

3
00:00:15,208 --> 00:00:18,500
<i>The butterfly perches on a horn!</i>

4
00:00:18,583 --> 00:00:21,583
<i>Search for gold until you're torn!</i>

5
00:00:33,875 --> 00:00:35,041
Smash it!

6
00:00:40,333 --> 00:00:43,208
Good afternoon, ladies and gentlemen.

7
00:00:43,291 --> 00:00:48,958
For those of you who have just arrived,
welcome to Bondan's Trance School party.

8
00:00:49,791 --> 00:00:52,708
Today, we're invoking
the butterfly spirit,

9
00:00:52,791 --> 00:00:55,583
the mouse deer spirit,
and the horse spirit.

10
00:00:55,666 --> 00:00:59,833
For those of you who wish to be possessed,
please approach us.

11
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:05,125
Today's trance leader is Mr. Yoga Nugraha.

12
00:01:07,333 --> 00:01:13,958
You may also approach his assistants,
Pawit Arifin, who is playing the guitar,

13
00:01:14,583 --> 00:01:19,708
or Bayu Laksana, who is playing the flute.

14
00:01:20,416 --> 00:01:24,458
And of course, we have a mantra today.

15
00:01:24,541 --> 00:01:27,958
In the hallucination realm,
everything is under the care

16
00:01:28,041 --> 00:01:32,833
of our trance school leader,
Mr. Bondan Junaedi.

17
00:01:34,875 --> 00:01:39,083
We would also like to thank
the head of Sentum Village

18
00:01:39,166 --> 00:01:43,500
for inviting Bondan's Trance School
from Latas Village

19
00:01:43,583 --> 00:01:50,208
to celebrate
Sentum Village's successful harvest.

20
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,416
Please join us,
don't just stay on the sidelines.

21
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:56,083
Come to the middle.

22
00:01:56,166 --> 00:02:02,458
If you have been fasting,
come and experience the butterfly spirit.

23
00:02:04,208 --> 00:02:07,375
This spirit is not just any spirit.

24
00:02:07,458 --> 00:02:11,250
It was conjured up
straight from Latas Village's spring.

25
00:02:12,416 --> 00:02:17,083
The spirit will bring color to your lives,
ladies and gentlemen.

26
00:02:17,958 --> 00:02:19,458
A meadow full of flowers.

27
00:02:20,083 --> 00:02:21,708
Go ahead and give it a try.

28
00:02:22,375 --> 00:02:25,375
If you haven't fasted,
but have been doing this for a while,

29
00:02:25,458 --> 00:02:28,583
you may also join in, don't be shy.

30
00:02:29,708 --> 00:02:36,708
Together, let's forget for a second
about work, loans, family problems.

31
00:02:37,583 --> 00:02:41,083
Enter the hallucination realm
and let it all go.

32
00:02:41,708 --> 00:02:45,583
Be one with the butterfly spirit.
Just like that.

33
00:02:47,375 --> 00:02:48,333
Before I forget,

34
00:02:48,958 --> 00:02:55,583
let's also welcome Guru Asri,
the leader of the Central Trance School.

35
00:02:56,208 --> 00:03:00,541
Welcome to our trance party, ma'am.

36
00:03:08,208 --> 00:03:11,750
Why did you stop?
I'm looking for a new spirit channeler.

37
00:03:11,833 --> 00:03:15,500
Keep going.
Send her into the hallucination realm.

38
00:03:52,583 --> 00:03:55,375
Good. She's in.

39
00:03:56,833 --> 00:04:01,250
Now, just like a butterfly spirit,
extract the nectar from the flowers,

40
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:03,875
and let them drink.

41
00:04:04,708 --> 00:04:08,916
<i>Nectar, nectar, nectar.</i>

42
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,416
<i>Don't screw this up.</i>

43
00:04:12,125 --> 00:04:13,125
<i>Nectar…</i>

44
00:04:13,208 --> 00:04:14,666
<i>- Nectar…</i>
- Concentrate.

45
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:18,291
- <i>Nectar…</i>
- Focus on what the nectar looks like.

46
00:04:18,375 --> 00:04:20,458
Does he know what he's doing?

47
00:04:30,583 --> 00:04:33,125
<i>Nectar, nectar, nectar.</i>

48
00:04:33,208 --> 00:04:34,750
<i>Sausages. Damn it!</i>

49
00:04:38,166 --> 00:04:41,791
<i>Are you dumb?</i>
<i>If you want a sausage, you can have one.</i>

50
00:04:41,875 --> 00:04:44,541
<i>But don't bring them</i>
<i>into the hallucination realm.</i>

51
00:04:44,625 --> 00:04:45,666
<i>Focus!</i>

52
00:04:49,250 --> 00:04:52,166
<i>Nectar, nectar, sweet nectar.</i>

53
00:04:59,583 --> 00:05:02,333
<i>Nectar, nectar, nectar.</i>

54
00:05:02,416 --> 00:05:03,250
<i>Eggs!</i>

55
00:05:06,833 --> 00:05:09,500
<i>Think nectar, not eggs.</i>

56
00:05:11,291 --> 00:05:13,500
It's a butterfly spirit,
not a snake spirit!

57
00:05:13,583 --> 00:05:17,833
You can't even concentrate,
and you expect to be a spirit channeler?

58
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:24,125
<i>Nectar, nectar, nectar.</i>

59
00:05:24,208 --> 00:05:27,875
<i>Nectar, nectar, nectar.</i>

60
00:05:27,958 --> 00:05:29,375
<i>Don't turn into oil.</i>

61
00:05:29,458 --> 00:05:30,625
<i>Nectar, nectar, nectar.</i>

62
00:05:30,708 --> 00:05:31,958
<i>Don't turn into oil.</i>

63
00:05:32,041 --> 00:05:32,875
<i>Nectar, nectar…</i>

64
00:05:32,958 --> 00:05:34,208
<i>Oil!</i>

65
00:05:40,708 --> 00:05:42,708
You're hurting them. Back off!

66
00:05:50,416 --> 00:05:52,666
<i>Oil burns the heart!</i>

67
00:05:52,750 --> 00:05:55,708
<i>Turn it into nectar!</i>

68
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:18,333
Please forgive my student, ma'am.

69
00:06:19,583 --> 00:06:22,166
Bayu, you idiot. Get out of here!

70
00:06:28,083 --> 00:06:29,708
You can try again tomorrow.

71
00:06:35,083 --> 00:06:39,791
May I have your attention,
ladies and gentlemen?

72
00:06:39,875 --> 00:06:43,875
We are accepting donations
and contributions

73
00:06:43,958 --> 00:06:49,833
to stop Wanaria
from getting their hands on our spring.

74
00:06:49,916 --> 00:06:53,125
Thanks, sir. I'm just heading over there.

75
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:57,250
- Thank you so much!
- Bayu, where are you going?

76
00:06:58,500 --> 00:06:59,375
Miss.

77
00:06:59,458 --> 00:07:02,333
You were at the party, right?
I'd like to apologize.

78
00:07:03,125 --> 00:07:05,958
Were you hurt?
That was supposed to be nectar, not oil.

79
00:07:06,041 --> 00:07:09,583
Here, I got you this voucher
as a little compensation.

80
00:07:10,208 --> 00:07:13,250
- A voucher?
- Yes, you can use it for the next party.

81
00:07:13,333 --> 00:07:17,958
You won't have to pay for the entrance.
Just show them the butterfly tattoo.

82
00:07:19,333 --> 00:07:22,125
Can I also get your phone number
for our customer records?

83
00:07:23,750 --> 00:07:29,125
When does this voucher expire?
I may already be back in Jakarta by then.

84
00:07:29,208 --> 00:07:33,208
That's not a problem.
Jakarta is only two hours away from Latas.

85
00:07:35,333 --> 00:07:37,000
- 081…
- Yes?

86
00:07:37,083 --> 00:07:38,458
723…

87
00:07:39,166 --> 00:07:41,708
- You're not gonna write it down?
- I'll remember.

88
00:07:41,791 --> 00:07:43,791
- Seriously?
- Yes.

89
00:07:43,875 --> 00:07:46,458
081723857533.

90
00:07:47,125 --> 00:07:49,250
0817…

91
00:07:50,125 --> 00:07:52,250
23857533.

92
00:07:53,333 --> 00:07:55,333
- You're good.
- It's nothing.

93
00:07:55,416 --> 00:07:57,041
Sure you won't forget it?

94
00:07:57,125 --> 00:08:01,166
081723857533.

95
00:08:02,583 --> 00:08:04,208
Can I also have your name?

96
00:08:04,291 --> 00:08:09,000
I'll only tell you my name
if I get well compensated as a customer.

97
00:08:10,958 --> 00:08:13,083
Shit! Bayu, help! He's getting away!

98
00:08:13,166 --> 00:08:15,958
Thank you for coming
to Bondan's Trance School party.

99
00:08:16,041 --> 00:08:16,916
Take care!

100
00:08:17,583 --> 00:08:20,125
- Bayu!
- 081723857533.

101
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:21,791
- Bayu!
- Yes, yes, yes.

102
00:08:26,333 --> 00:08:27,791
Did you forget the rules?

103
00:08:28,625 --> 00:08:30,833
We can't let the spirit hosts get away.
Play!

104
00:08:30,916 --> 00:08:33,916
081723857533.

105
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,666
Was that a lotto number? Come on!

106
00:08:38,375 --> 00:08:42,458
- Guru Asri had her eye on me today.
- Don't get your hopes up.

107
00:08:43,666 --> 00:08:47,958
"Bayu Prasetya, featured by Asri's
Trance School, number one in Latas!"

108
00:08:48,833 --> 00:08:51,541
"Bayu Prasetya,
featured by Tono's Trance School,

109
00:08:51,625 --> 00:08:53,916
number 2000-964-33-267…"

110
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Shut up,
I'm trying to memorize her number!

111
00:08:56,083 --> 00:09:00,000
- 0817238…
- Seven! Three, two! One, one!

112
00:09:00,083 --> 00:09:01,166
Shut up.

113
00:09:01,250 --> 00:09:04,375
Hey, look!
They're turning your house into a hotel!

114
00:09:04,458 --> 00:09:07,625
And your house has been turned
into a golf course!

115
00:09:07,708 --> 00:09:09,958
You could use the money for your wedding!

116
00:09:10,041 --> 00:09:12,875
What a waste! Might as well
get a new pedal for my guitar!

117
00:09:12,958 --> 00:09:13,791
Asshole!

118
00:09:14,875 --> 00:09:17,833
- Go to hell, you bum!
- I am a bum.

119
00:09:31,750 --> 00:09:36,083
So, you can't use grasshoppers
as bait for catfish?

120
00:09:37,250 --> 00:09:39,458
No, we usually use tree worms.

121
00:09:40,625 --> 00:09:43,416
When it comes to snails,
we use feces as bait.

122
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:47,000
- Really?
- I mean human feces.

123
00:09:47,875 --> 00:09:48,833
Hey, Bayu.

124
00:09:48,916 --> 00:09:50,875
Mr. Fahri, this is my son.

125
00:09:50,958 --> 00:09:54,208
- Hello, Bayu. I'm Fahri.
- My hands are dirty.

126
00:09:54,291 --> 00:09:57,375
It's all right.
Dirty is another word for organic.

127
00:09:58,666 --> 00:10:01,166
You haven't been
catching snails, have you?

128
00:10:02,125 --> 00:10:03,750
- No.
- All good?

129
00:10:04,541 --> 00:10:06,500
- We'd better get going now.
- Okay.

130
00:10:06,583 --> 00:10:09,583
- Mr. Iwan, thank you for your time.
- Sure.

131
00:10:10,208 --> 00:10:13,000
- Keep me posted.
- Will do.

132
00:10:13,083 --> 00:10:14,250
- I'm serious.
- Yes.

133
00:10:14,333 --> 00:10:17,208
I'll be back next week
and I'll bring my rod.

134
00:10:17,291 --> 00:10:21,875
{\an8}I'll learn how to fish from you,
the fishing master.

135
00:10:21,958 --> 00:10:23,958
{\an8}Stop it. I just do it for fun.

136
00:10:24,041 --> 00:10:27,000
Bye, Bayu. See you.

137
00:10:28,208 --> 00:10:29,791
- Drive safe.
- Let's go.

138
00:10:29,875 --> 00:10:31,666
- Thank you.
- My pleasure.

139
00:10:32,708 --> 00:10:34,166
What did he want?

140
00:10:34,250 --> 00:10:38,041
Nothing, he just wanted
to ask me some questions about our land.

141
00:10:38,125 --> 00:10:39,666
- Why?
- Because of this.

142
00:10:40,666 --> 00:10:42,625
A new real estate project.

143
00:10:43,333 --> 00:10:45,708
{\an8}They're building houses
closer to our area.

144
00:10:45,791 --> 00:10:48,250
- Where are we going to live then?
- Here.

145
00:10:50,333 --> 00:10:53,333
A brand new apartment building
close to the train station.

146
00:10:54,083 --> 00:10:57,791
You wanna go back to Jakarta?
Back to eating once every two days?

147
00:10:57,875 --> 00:11:01,250
Well, a friend of mine
asked me to join her business.

148
00:11:01,333 --> 00:11:02,958
Bottled water dispensers.

149
00:11:05,083 --> 00:11:06,583
We'll break even in no time.

150
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:11,625
What if it fails, like the silver jewelry
business you had with your other friend?

151
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:14,541
I ended up working as a street performer.

152
00:11:14,625 --> 00:11:16,333
It's still under discussion.

153
00:11:17,375 --> 00:11:18,791
Just relax and eat something.

154
00:11:18,875 --> 00:11:21,541
I have to fast.
I'm getting ready to catch some spirits.

155
00:11:21,625 --> 00:11:23,666
Catch spirits? You're a musician.

156
00:11:23,750 --> 00:11:28,541
Guru Asri came to the trance party today.
She saw me play and seemed interested.

157
00:11:28,625 --> 00:11:32,041
From the Central Trance School?
So you'll get paid better?

158
00:11:32,125 --> 00:11:33,666
I have to be selected first.

159
00:11:33,750 --> 00:11:35,833
That's why I need to practice
for tomorrow.

160
00:11:35,916 --> 00:11:40,250
I thought you wanted to eat every day,
but now you're fasting willingly.

161
00:11:40,333 --> 00:11:43,500
- I don't get it.
- The difference is now it's my choice.

162
00:11:43,583 --> 00:11:46,541
In Jakarta, it was because
debt collectors were stalking us.

163
00:11:46,625 --> 00:11:48,500
Don't sell the house, okay?

164
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:51,000
This is my chance to earn a living here.

165
00:11:51,083 --> 00:11:53,250
After this,
I'll be able to provide for you.

166
00:11:53,333 --> 00:11:55,500
I'm not gonna suffer again in Jakarta.

167
00:12:03,375 --> 00:12:04,583
This company

168
00:12:05,375 --> 00:12:09,333
is trying to buy Mr. Dawuri's
spirit spring and turn it into a hotel.

169
00:12:10,041 --> 00:12:13,208
That means no more spirits.
No more trance parties.

170
00:12:13,291 --> 00:12:15,375
No more jobs for us.

171
00:12:15,458 --> 00:12:16,625
The problem is,

172
00:12:18,041 --> 00:12:21,958
Mr. Dawuri has a grandson
with brain cancer.

173
00:12:23,625 --> 00:12:26,875
They need 250 million rupiah
for his surgery.

174
00:12:26,958 --> 00:12:30,416
Wanaria has offered him
300 million for his spring.

175
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:34,708
Our trance school has negotiated
for 250 million.

176
00:12:36,375 --> 00:12:38,208
Thankfully, Mr. Dawuri agreed.

177
00:12:38,291 --> 00:12:40,041
So, next month,

178
00:12:40,125 --> 00:12:43,458
Central Trance School will have
a big fundraising trance party.

179
00:12:44,458 --> 00:12:46,625
And we need a new spirit channeler.

180
00:12:46,708 --> 00:12:48,875
He has to be the best in Latas,

181
00:12:48,958 --> 00:12:51,958
because they convinced
our previous spirit channeler

182
00:12:52,041 --> 00:12:54,000
to sell his land and move to Jakarta.

183
00:12:54,583 --> 00:12:55,916
Form a circle for the host!

184
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,708
Forming the circle!

185
00:12:59,791 --> 00:13:03,708
Forming the circle!

186
00:13:08,958 --> 00:13:11,416
This baby monkey spirit needs comforting.

187
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:17,958
Whoever gets the monkey
to hug the wooden beam, wins.

188
00:13:18,041 --> 00:13:20,125
You're all spirit-channeler candidates.

189
00:13:21,083 --> 00:13:23,958
Can you make this host feel good?

190
00:13:25,125 --> 00:13:26,583
Get ready!

191
00:13:29,708 --> 00:13:30,833
Begin!

192
00:13:44,333 --> 00:13:45,666
Concentrate.

193
00:13:50,708 --> 00:13:51,875
Focus.

194
00:13:55,208 --> 00:13:58,625
Draw him toward your sound.

195
00:14:02,708 --> 00:14:05,000
Like all living beings,

196
00:14:06,333 --> 00:14:08,541
humans also need to hug each other.

197
00:14:11,333 --> 00:14:15,083
At least six times a day.

198
00:14:15,833 --> 00:14:20,125
Hugging reduces stress
and makes you live longer.

199
00:14:20,208 --> 00:14:24,541
<i>Be a fluffy stuffed animal.</i>
<i>Be a fluffy stuffed animal.</i>

200
00:14:32,333 --> 00:14:36,875
No matter how big or small
this village's problems are,

201
00:14:36,958 --> 00:14:40,333
as long as we hug each other,

202
00:14:41,125 --> 00:14:43,041
we'll overcome all of them!

203
00:14:44,708 --> 00:14:45,916
<i>Problems.</i>

204
00:14:46,250 --> 00:14:47,708
<i>Problems.</i>

205
00:14:47,791 --> 00:14:49,958
<i>Dad is going to sell the house to Wanaria.</i>

206
00:14:50,583 --> 00:14:51,875
<i>Shut up!</i>

207
00:14:51,958 --> 00:14:53,416
<i>We'll be homeless again.</i>

208
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:54,833
<i>Shut up!</i>

209
00:15:00,833 --> 00:15:02,000
Focus.

210
00:15:03,791 --> 00:15:04,666
Concentrate.

211
00:15:05,750 --> 00:15:08,750
<i>After they buy the house,</i>
<i>they'll tear it down.</i>

212
00:15:08,833 --> 00:15:10,250
<i>This is all Fahri's fault.</i>

213
00:15:12,833 --> 00:15:13,875
Focus.

214
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:18,041
Get rid of all the anger and resentment.

215
00:15:28,583 --> 00:15:34,000
Achieving a state of trance
is all about channeling happiness.

216
00:15:34,083 --> 00:15:38,083
<i>Be happy, be joyful, be grateful.</i>

217
00:15:38,166 --> 00:15:39,916
<i>Be hugged by the stuffed animal.</i>

218
00:15:51,125 --> 00:15:53,500
Two musicians are fighting
for the monkey's hug.

219
00:15:53,583 --> 00:15:56,333
The baby monkey
can sense who's the most comforting,

220
00:15:56,958 --> 00:16:00,500
who can make him feel safest,

221
00:16:00,583 --> 00:16:04,166
who can give him the most warmth,

222
00:16:04,250 --> 00:16:07,500
who can best protect him from evil beings.

223
00:16:07,583 --> 00:16:10,291
This will show us
who's got the purest heart.

224
00:16:11,500 --> 00:16:15,208
We'll feel the love you all have to give.

225
00:16:15,291 --> 00:16:20,000
Focus all your love,
visualize it, and let it out!

226
00:16:20,083 --> 00:16:22,000
Channel it!

227
00:16:27,083 --> 00:16:28,041
Stop!

228
00:16:35,708 --> 00:16:39,166
For tomorrow,
you have to bring a spirit and a host.

229
00:16:39,250 --> 00:16:40,750
Do you have them?

230
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:42,916
- No, ma'am.
- Go find them, then.

231
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:44,541
Do it tonight.

232
00:16:45,125 --> 00:16:48,250
Remember,
you have to be one with the spirit.

233
00:16:48,333 --> 00:16:49,958
- Got it?
- Got it, ma'am.

234
00:16:58,291 --> 00:17:00,458
Getting a head start
for the selection, I see.

235
00:17:02,166 --> 00:17:04,875
Excuse us, Mr. Dawuri.
We're looking for some spirits.

236
00:17:04,958 --> 00:17:06,000
Go ahead!

237
00:17:06,083 --> 00:17:07,541
What's Wanaria doing here?

238
00:17:07,625 --> 00:17:10,833
You think Mr. Dawuri will cave in?
Wanaria offers good money.

239
00:17:11,625 --> 00:17:13,458
It's up to his family, I guess.

240
00:17:17,625 --> 00:17:19,583
<i>The one at the spring, monitor?</i>

241
00:17:19,666 --> 00:17:22,666
Let's go down to the other spring.
No one's there yet.

242
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:24,416
<i>Should I send you some coffee?</i>

243
00:17:25,250 --> 00:17:27,375
Those assholes from Wanaria are too close.

244
00:17:27,458 --> 00:17:30,250
But if you focus,
you'll still be able to catch the spirit.

245
00:17:31,166 --> 00:17:32,000
Ready?

246
00:17:32,916 --> 00:17:35,666
First, visualize the throne.

247
00:17:35,750 --> 00:17:40,333
<i>Has it been connected</i>
<i>to the battery yet, sir?</i>

248
00:17:45,416 --> 00:17:47,708
Can you see a white throne?

249
00:17:56,083 --> 00:17:58,125
Invite the spirit to sit on the throne.

250
00:17:59,125 --> 00:17:59,958
Come on.

251
00:18:02,458 --> 00:18:03,875
<i>Relax.</i>

252
00:18:04,708 --> 00:18:06,541
<i>Concentrate.</i>

253
00:18:08,083 --> 00:18:10,333
<i>Mouse deer team, do you copy?</i>

254
00:18:11,083 --> 00:18:13,000
<i>Mouse deer team here, go ahead.</i>

255
00:18:13,083 --> 00:18:17,208
<i>Have you memorized Wanaria's song?</i>
<i>You need to know it by Monday.</i>

256
00:18:18,250 --> 00:18:22,583
<i>Okay, we're going to rehearse it.</i>
<i>Can you play it to us, sir?</i>

257
00:18:23,208 --> 00:18:25,083
<i>Copy that.</i>

258
00:18:25,833 --> 00:18:29,083
<i>Okay, I just got it. Playing it now.</i>

259
00:18:34,333 --> 00:18:39,750
<i>Life is better in the land of Wanaria</i>

260
00:18:39,833 --> 00:18:45,416
<i>We'll protect it until the end of time</i>

261
00:18:47,208 --> 00:18:52,208
<i>The Mighty Guard, that's us</i>

262
00:18:53,541 --> 00:18:56,333
<i>My body and soul…</i>

263
00:18:57,333 --> 00:18:59,000
<i>Concentrate.</i>

264
00:18:59,083 --> 00:19:01,000
<i>Ignore those voices.</i>

265
00:19:01,625 --> 00:19:05,708
<i>Focus on your breathing.</i>

266
00:19:32,583 --> 00:19:37,458
<i>Focus. Turn off all your senses.</i>

267
00:19:49,250 --> 00:19:52,625
<i>Focus, focus, focus. Don't get distracted.</i>

268
00:19:52,708 --> 00:19:56,625
<i>Ignore the smells. Ignore the voices.</i>

269
00:19:56,708 --> 00:19:59,583
<i>Ignore the smells. Ignore the voices.</i>

270
00:20:01,291 --> 00:20:05,333
Remember,
you have to be one with the spirit.

271
00:20:14,333 --> 00:20:15,333
A turtle?

272
00:20:25,083 --> 00:20:26,750
Pawit, help me.

273
00:20:34,125 --> 00:20:35,458
<i>Become a turtle.</i>

274
00:20:36,958 --> 00:20:38,750
<i>A turtle inside its shell.</i>

275
00:20:40,250 --> 00:20:43,375
<i>Inside its shell,</i>
<i>a turtle can't hear anything.</i>

276
00:20:43,458 --> 00:20:46,666
<i>Inside its shell,</i>
<i>a turtle can't see anything.</i>

277
00:20:47,458 --> 00:20:51,041
<i>Inside its shell, a turtle feels safe.</i>

278
00:20:55,083 --> 00:20:57,250
<i>The throne is clear.</i>

279
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:01,000
<i>I'm ready to receive the spirit.</i>

280
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:30,958
Did you catch it?

281
00:21:32,166 --> 00:21:33,333
Did you catch it or not?

282
00:21:39,791 --> 00:21:40,791
Excuse me, miss.

283
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:46,541
Bondan's Trance School
wants to give you this free chicken soup

284
00:21:46,625 --> 00:21:48,833
as an apology for what happened
the other day.

285
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:52,625
Are you blind? This is a chicken farm.

286
00:21:52,708 --> 00:21:55,250
If the chickens smell that soup,
they'll go nuts.

287
00:21:55,333 --> 00:21:56,666
- Really?
- Who let you in?

288
00:21:56,750 --> 00:21:59,541
- I'm calling security.
- I'm sorry! I didn't know!

289
00:22:00,750 --> 00:22:02,666
I'm just kidding, chill.

290
00:22:03,708 --> 00:22:04,833
Damn.

291
00:22:05,500 --> 00:22:08,041
You think you're a comedian, don't you?

292
00:22:08,125 --> 00:22:12,666
I have another voucher for you.

293
00:22:12,750 --> 00:22:15,541
Another voucher?
What are you, an online shop?

294
00:22:15,625 --> 00:22:17,375
This is a VIP voucher.

295
00:22:17,458 --> 00:22:20,541
You get free access to our rehearsal
and sound check.

296
00:22:20,625 --> 00:22:23,083
Do you work as a K-pop event
promoter or something?

297
00:22:23,166 --> 00:22:25,791
No, not K-pop.

298
00:22:25,875 --> 00:22:29,708
What other trance parties
have you attended?

299
00:22:30,291 --> 00:22:31,541
Bondan,

300
00:22:33,458 --> 00:22:34,583
Tono…

301
00:22:35,208 --> 00:22:37,041
What's the other one? Oh! Wati.

302
00:22:37,708 --> 00:22:39,041
Only those three.

303
00:22:39,125 --> 00:22:42,916
The school I'm with now
is the best of them all.

304
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:47,500
I'd like to invite you
to be my practice partner.

305
00:22:48,208 --> 00:22:50,250
I'll give you free tickets to parties.

306
00:22:50,333 --> 00:22:52,208
- For real?
- Yeah.

307
00:22:54,583 --> 00:22:55,416
When?

308
00:22:56,333 --> 00:22:57,166
Tomorrow.

309
00:23:02,583 --> 00:23:04,083
Okay.

310
00:23:04,166 --> 00:23:05,166
Really?

311
00:23:05,833 --> 00:23:07,083
Awesome.

312
00:23:08,208 --> 00:23:11,041
But 12 hours before, you have to…

313
00:23:11,125 --> 00:23:13,458
{\an8}Fast. I know.

314
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:17,750
So what's the soup for, then?

315
00:23:19,416 --> 00:23:20,583
Good question.

316
00:23:21,833 --> 00:23:24,416
Can I have your name?

317
00:23:24,500 --> 00:23:26,833
It's for the guest book
for tomorrow's party.

318
00:23:26,916 --> 00:23:30,625
Asking for customers' names, again?
Is it a school or a coffee shop?

319
00:23:30,708 --> 00:23:31,541
Here.

320
00:23:32,833 --> 00:23:33,750
All right.

321
00:23:33,833 --> 00:23:37,083
Thank you, Laksmi. I'm Bayu.

322
00:23:37,166 --> 00:23:38,166
See you then.

323
00:23:40,333 --> 00:23:42,208
See you tomorrow, Laksmi.

324
00:23:42,958 --> 00:23:44,166
- Yes.
- See you.

325
00:23:57,750 --> 00:23:59,125
- Bayu.
- I'm heading out, Dad.

326
00:23:59,791 --> 00:24:02,750
- This is an old friend of mine.
- Hello, handsome.

327
00:24:02,833 --> 00:24:04,291
- Bayu.
- Bayu.

328
00:24:04,375 --> 00:24:08,083
Excuse me, ma'am.
I have to go to work. Goodbye.

329
00:24:08,166 --> 00:24:11,291
Wait, Bayu. I have a present for you.

330
00:24:13,458 --> 00:24:15,916
Ta-da!

331
00:24:17,375 --> 00:24:19,083
Isn't it great?

332
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:21,500
For you to practice.

333
00:24:22,333 --> 00:24:23,500
Practice for what?

334
00:24:23,583 --> 00:24:27,791
When your father opens his water
dispenser business in Jakarta,

335
00:24:27,875 --> 00:24:31,333
you can use this motorcycle
to deliver the bottles.

336
00:24:31,958 --> 00:24:32,958
Water bottles?

337
00:24:33,041 --> 00:24:36,375
Your father said Wanaria
has made him an offer on this house.

338
00:24:36,458 --> 00:24:38,666
It's good money.

339
00:24:38,750 --> 00:24:41,416
It's just an idea, Bayu.

340
00:24:42,708 --> 00:24:44,125
Thanks, ma'am,

341
00:24:45,250 --> 00:24:49,041
but I already have a job here
and I'm not planning to leave.

342
00:24:49,625 --> 00:24:52,458
- Dad, where's my bike?
- Mrs. Nana's son took it for a ride.

343
00:24:52,541 --> 00:24:56,375
Take the motorcycle. It's faster.
Let me show you.

344
00:24:56,458 --> 00:25:00,000
Don't knock it until you've tried it.
You'll like it.

345
00:25:04,250 --> 00:25:06,333
Okay? Here you go.

346
00:25:06,416 --> 00:25:08,708
Mouse deer on a small tree branch!

347
00:25:08,791 --> 00:25:11,166
Pay your debt and leave nothing to chance!

348
00:25:23,083 --> 00:25:24,083
Concentrate.

349
00:25:25,458 --> 00:25:27,000
Come on, focus.

350
00:25:27,083 --> 00:25:29,583
Channel the joy.
Don't think about anything else.

351
00:25:30,333 --> 00:25:33,250
Mr. Damar, Mrs. Rosita,
and Mr. Prapto are with us today.

352
00:25:33,333 --> 00:25:37,583
They are former spirit channelers
who will be the judges for the selection.

353
00:25:37,666 --> 00:25:40,000
We will be evaluating your performance.

354
00:25:54,208 --> 00:25:57,208
There are 20 spirits in this village.

355
00:25:58,458 --> 00:26:02,500
{\an8}If you're not sure
about the spirit you have now,

356
00:26:03,208 --> 00:26:04,875
replace it with another one.

357
00:26:19,958 --> 00:26:23,750
Sorry. A Wanaria bulldozer
was blocking the road.

358
00:26:23,833 --> 00:26:24,708
It's fine.

359
00:26:31,375 --> 00:26:33,458
- Tutik from Maryana.
- What's your spirit?

360
00:26:33,541 --> 00:26:34,375
The finch, ma'am.

361
00:26:34,458 --> 00:26:37,333
Perched on the rain gutter it tweets!

362
00:26:37,416 --> 00:26:39,958
A sweet tweet! A sweet tweet!

363
00:26:53,625 --> 00:26:56,583
Play something more soothing
and melodious. Don't lose it.

364
00:26:56,666 --> 00:27:00,291
Today, there are eight candidates
from eight schools in Latas.

365
00:27:00,375 --> 00:27:05,833
The two candidates with the lowest scores
will be eliminated.

366
00:27:06,791 --> 00:27:11,458
The top three candidates
will move on to the final selection.

367
00:27:13,416 --> 00:27:14,333
Hey, kid.

368
00:27:15,583 --> 00:27:17,000
What's your name, again?

369
00:27:18,041 --> 00:27:19,291
That's right, Bayu!

370
00:27:20,583 --> 00:27:22,375
- That's me.
- Yes.

371
00:27:22,458 --> 00:27:24,458
I saw you yesterday.

372
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:27,250
That was amazing.

373
00:27:28,541 --> 00:27:30,250
Amazing how bad you suck.

374
00:27:33,791 --> 00:27:36,000
- Record me, will you?
- Sure.

375
00:27:42,958 --> 00:27:45,416
I am Ananto from Ningsih's school!

376
00:27:45,500 --> 00:27:47,541
- What's your spirit?
- The ant.

377
00:27:48,375 --> 00:27:50,750
Fire ant! Burn! Burn! Burn!

378
00:27:50,833 --> 00:27:54,208
His hair will return!

379
00:28:13,333 --> 00:28:16,083
Teachers and spirit channelers
work as one.

380
00:28:16,833 --> 00:28:18,583
The teachers create the realm,

381
00:28:18,666 --> 00:28:21,083
and the spirit channelers
bring it to life.

382
00:28:34,958 --> 00:28:35,958
Next!

383
00:28:45,083 --> 00:28:46,875
I'm Bayu from Bondan's school.

384
00:28:46,958 --> 00:28:48,833
- What's your spirit?
- The turtle.

385
00:28:49,833 --> 00:28:51,166
Geez.

386
00:28:52,458 --> 00:28:53,875
Don't be rude.

387
00:28:53,958 --> 00:28:56,708
What's wrong with bringing
the most basic spirit?

388
00:28:56,791 --> 00:29:00,250
Even my kid in grade school
can get that one.

389
00:29:00,333 --> 00:29:03,208
No wonder he was late.
He's as slow as a turtle.

390
00:29:05,791 --> 00:29:08,666
Don't mind them. They don't mean any harm.

391
00:29:08,750 --> 00:29:11,833
Those percussionists
have looked after me since I was a kid.

392
00:29:12,958 --> 00:29:18,583
Okay, I'll create a special place
for Bayu the Turtle.

393
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:30,000
The turtle wrapped around a whale!

394
00:29:30,083 --> 00:29:32,458
Hard-shelled, soft as hair!

395
00:29:51,833 --> 00:29:54,833
<i>The turtle</i>
<i>tucks itself into its shell to rest.</i>

396
00:29:55,708 --> 00:29:57,708
<i>How will you, Bayu the Turtle,</i>

397
00:29:57,791 --> 00:30:00,666
<i>make the host feel comfortable</i>
<i>inside that shell?</i>

398
00:30:02,500 --> 00:30:03,916
Tough as a rattan tree!

399
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:07,375
Let's see how thick the turtle's shell is.

400
00:30:24,041 --> 00:30:26,458
<i>You can hit her all you want.</i>

401
00:30:26,541 --> 00:30:32,208
<i>As long as the turtle's in its shell,</i>
<i>it'll feel like a gentle massage to her.</i>

402
00:30:36,875 --> 00:30:39,125
Someone's getting distracted.

403
00:30:39,208 --> 00:30:42,916
<i>Focus on massaging Laksmi.</i>

404
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:46,875
<i>Don't think about anything else.</i>

405
00:30:46,958 --> 00:30:47,791
<i>Shit.</i>

406
00:30:48,583 --> 00:30:50,208
{\an8}Hello, Bayu.

407
00:30:57,083 --> 00:30:58,958
What's on your mind, boy?

408
00:30:59,833 --> 00:31:00,916
Focus!

409
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:04,250
If your thoughts waver,
she could actually get caned.

410
00:31:04,333 --> 00:31:08,125
<i>Concentrate. Dad won't remarry.</i>

411
00:31:08,208 --> 00:31:09,375
Bayu?

412
00:31:09,458 --> 00:31:11,000
Your tune is shaky.

413
00:31:11,083 --> 00:31:13,000
<i>Get rid of all made-up thoughts.</i>

414
00:31:13,083 --> 00:31:16,000
<i>Dad won't run a water dispenser business</i>
<i>with Mrs. Nana.</i>

415
00:31:17,625 --> 00:31:20,750
<i>Come, my boy.</i>
<i>Help mama refill the water bottle.</i>

416
00:31:21,541 --> 00:31:24,250
If your mind wanders off,
that girl could get hurt!

417
00:31:31,541 --> 00:31:36,625
<i>Focus, focus, focus.</i>
<i>Stay in the hallucination realm.</i>

418
00:31:36,708 --> 00:31:39,958
<i>Come, my boy.</i>
<i>Help mama refill the water bottle.</i>

419
00:31:40,041 --> 00:31:45,833
<i>Come, my boy.</i>
<i>Help mama refill the water bottle.</i>

420
00:31:50,041 --> 00:31:52,125
{\an8}- Laksmi!
- Wait!

421
00:31:52,208 --> 00:31:53,041
Laksmi!

422
00:32:02,625 --> 00:32:07,666
The sound of your flute tells me
you're having family problems.

423
00:32:07,750 --> 00:32:11,208
We keep no secrets in this school.

424
00:32:12,083 --> 00:32:14,500
We can help you resolve
your concentration issues.

425
00:32:14,583 --> 00:32:15,833
Now, tell me honestly.

426
00:32:17,875 --> 00:32:19,750
What were you thinking about?

427
00:32:23,250 --> 00:32:25,500
Tell me.

428
00:32:25,583 --> 00:32:27,583
I was thinking about my father.

429
00:32:28,583 --> 00:32:30,750
What about your father?

430
00:32:30,833 --> 00:32:33,625
My father wants me to get married.

431
00:32:33,708 --> 00:32:36,750
Liar, liar.

432
00:32:37,708 --> 00:32:42,125
If I can hear your tune wavering,
your lies are also clear to my ears.

433
00:32:42,208 --> 00:32:43,208
Tell me the truth!

434
00:32:45,458 --> 00:32:46,333
My father…

435
00:32:47,500 --> 00:32:50,541
wants me to move to Jakarta
and help with his water business.

436
00:32:52,625 --> 00:32:55,583
- With what money?
- A loan from the bank.

437
00:32:56,708 --> 00:32:59,625
Liar, liar.

438
00:32:59,708 --> 00:33:02,416
You already lied twice, boy!

439
00:33:02,500 --> 00:33:04,416
You don't think I can see through it?

440
00:33:05,625 --> 00:33:10,250
A liar is someone
who can't accept who he is.

441
00:33:10,333 --> 00:33:15,333
So how can he channel spirits
for other people?

442
00:33:18,375 --> 00:33:20,375
He'll get the money…

443
00:33:21,500 --> 00:33:22,791
by selling the house.

444
00:33:24,041 --> 00:33:26,250
- Traitor!
- Wanaria's pet!

445
00:33:26,333 --> 00:33:30,583
Why did your father
have to resort to selling the house?

446
00:33:30,666 --> 00:33:34,083
He doesn't have a job.
No one will hire him.

447
00:33:34,958 --> 00:33:36,125
Why is that?

448
00:33:38,583 --> 00:33:41,458
{\an8}He stole a phone and went to jail.

449
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:45,333
What does your mother do?

450
00:33:48,500 --> 00:33:50,333
{\an8}She married a picture framer.

451
00:33:52,083 --> 00:33:56,125
Is she happy with that man?

452
00:33:56,208 --> 00:33:57,333
Yes!

453
00:33:58,625 --> 00:34:01,000
Is your father happy?

454
00:34:01,083 --> 00:34:02,208
No!

455
00:34:03,208 --> 00:34:05,375
Are you happy?

456
00:34:05,458 --> 00:34:06,375
No!

457
00:34:06,458 --> 00:34:11,625
If you're not happy, do you think
you can channel happiness for others?

458
00:34:11,708 --> 00:34:12,583
No!

459
00:34:13,375 --> 00:34:16,000
Can you change the past?

460
00:34:16,083 --> 00:34:17,000
No!

461
00:34:17,833 --> 00:34:20,500
Have you made peace with the past?

462
00:34:20,583 --> 00:34:21,916
No!

463
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:29,000
If you're not at peace with the past,
how can you be happy?

464
00:34:33,625 --> 00:34:34,708
{\an8}Judges,

465
00:34:35,875 --> 00:34:37,833
who got the highest score today?

466
00:34:38,583 --> 00:34:40,833
Ananto got the highest score.

467
00:34:43,166 --> 00:34:45,458
The bottom two were Sulis…

468
00:34:47,208 --> 00:34:49,166
And Sigit.

469
00:34:53,583 --> 00:34:55,875
Make peace with what has happened.

470
00:34:57,708 --> 00:35:02,333
If you can't do that, you can forget
about becoming a spirit channeler.

471
00:35:03,083 --> 00:35:05,458
Just help your father with his business.

472
00:35:05,541 --> 00:35:08,208
Or sell picture frames,
like your stepfather.

473
00:35:12,250 --> 00:35:15,250
<i>That one goes to the right,</i>
<i>and I want that one on the left.</i>

474
00:35:15,333 --> 00:35:18,458
- Yes, it has more space now.
<i>- That one looks good there.</i>

475
00:35:18,541 --> 00:35:19,958
This isn't what I want.

476
00:35:20,041 --> 00:35:20,958
<i>Okay.</i>

477
00:35:21,666 --> 00:35:22,666
Bayu.

478
00:35:23,250 --> 00:35:26,083
We might never get
another opportunity like this.

479
00:35:26,166 --> 00:35:29,500
We can't always depend
on Uncle Rahmat's monthly allowance.

480
00:35:29,583 --> 00:35:34,000
If the water business goes well,
you won't have to suffer like now.

481
00:35:34,083 --> 00:35:37,250
Suffer? I actually enjoy
working at the trance school.

482
00:35:37,333 --> 00:35:40,416
And I can still afford
to buy us food every day.

483
00:35:40,500 --> 00:35:43,625
I've been buying enough food
for three meals a day.

484
00:35:43,708 --> 00:35:45,416
But it's always the same food.

485
00:35:45,500 --> 00:35:47,458
Don't you want to live more comfortably?

486
00:35:47,541 --> 00:35:51,208
You want to eat something different?
Fine, I'll get it for you.

487
00:35:52,625 --> 00:35:55,250
I have to fast anyway.
I only eat once a day.

488
00:35:55,333 --> 00:35:56,875
What more do you want?

489
00:35:56,958 --> 00:35:59,625
In the city, we'll have to live
in a tiny, stuffy place.

490
00:35:59,708 --> 00:36:01,833
If you fail,
the debt collectors will come.

491
00:36:01,916 --> 00:36:04,375
You'll take out more loans
and drown in debt.

492
00:36:04,458 --> 00:36:07,875
{\an8}Listen, if we move to the city,

493
00:36:07,958 --> 00:36:10,625
{\an8}you can pursue your dream
and study hospitality.

494
00:36:10,708 --> 00:36:12,208
{\an8}I don't want that anymore.

495
00:36:12,291 --> 00:36:15,250
I'll be a spirit channeler
at Asri's school.

496
00:36:15,333 --> 00:36:17,583
I'll make as much money
as Nana's business.

497
00:36:17,666 --> 00:36:21,125
Tell Uncle Rahmat
not to send any more money next month.

498
00:36:21,208 --> 00:36:22,791
What if you don't get selected?

499
00:36:22,875 --> 00:36:25,250
There are a lot of people
who are better than you.

500
00:36:25,333 --> 00:36:26,875
I will be selected!

501
00:36:26,958 --> 00:36:30,750
I've been practicing for years.
Don't ruin what I've accomplished so far.

502
00:36:30,833 --> 00:36:33,625
But I'm not the only owner of this house.

503
00:36:33,708 --> 00:36:38,333
It's also Uncle Rahmat's and Aunt Wati's.
Your grandmother split it among us.

504
00:36:38,416 --> 00:36:43,958
Fine, then don't say anything.
Don't tell them about Fahri's offer.

505
00:36:44,041 --> 00:36:47,375
We can use my spirit-channeler salary
to pay off the house

506
00:36:47,458 --> 00:36:49,625
so it can be all ours.

507
00:36:49,708 --> 00:36:52,250
How long will you be out catching spirits?

508
00:36:52,333 --> 00:36:55,750
Next week, we have to go to Jakarta
to see Rahmat's new granddaughter.

509
00:36:55,833 --> 00:36:59,083
Yes, I know.
Just don't tell them anything.

510
00:37:02,333 --> 00:37:06,125
<i>The goat, the bedbug and the grasshopper</i>
<i>are mid-rank spirits in Latas.</i>

511
00:37:06,208 --> 00:37:12,375
<i>To catch them, one must suffer,</i>
<i>fast, and live like those animals do.</i>

512
00:37:12,458 --> 00:37:16,291
<i>The more we behave like them,</i>
<i>the faster they will come to us.</i>

513
00:37:28,708 --> 00:37:35,250
<i>Empty, empty, empty.</i>

514
00:37:35,333 --> 00:37:39,416
<i>Empty, empty, empty.</i>

515
00:37:57,916 --> 00:38:00,333
<i>Calm, calm, calm.</i>

516
00:38:24,750 --> 00:38:30,875
<i>Relax, relax, relax.</i>

517
00:38:41,750 --> 00:38:45,291
<i>Get out of my head. Get out of my head.</i>

518
00:38:45,375 --> 00:38:47,541
<i>Noisy, noisy, noisy.</i>

519
00:38:47,625 --> 00:38:53,541
<i>Get out of my head. Get out of my head.</i>

520
00:39:13,500 --> 00:39:17,375
<i>Blood rushes to the head.</i>
<i>Blood rushes to the head.</i>

521
00:39:18,208 --> 00:39:20,083
<i>Blood rushes to the head.</i>

522
00:39:45,041 --> 00:39:46,083
<i>Relax.</i>

523
00:39:47,666 --> 00:39:49,166
<i>My mind is empty.</i>

524
00:39:51,666 --> 00:39:53,958
<i>I'm ready to receive the spirit.</i>

525
00:39:56,458 --> 00:39:58,833
<i>I'm ready to receive the spirit.</i>

526
00:40:01,208 --> 00:40:04,083
<i>I'm ready to receive the spirit.</i>

527
00:40:06,083 --> 00:40:08,583
<i>I'm ready to receive the spirit.</i>

528
00:40:11,625 --> 00:40:12,500
Hello.

529
00:40:14,000 --> 00:40:17,625
What kind of meditation technique
are you practicing?

530
00:40:18,208 --> 00:40:23,875
Sorry, but you will have to move
because we're cutting down the trees.

531
00:40:24,708 --> 00:40:25,541
I'm sorry.

532
00:40:59,583 --> 00:41:02,541
That new spirit feels good.

533
00:41:03,333 --> 00:41:07,500
I didn't think I could get possessed
without Guru Asri's mantra.

534
00:41:08,208 --> 00:41:10,958
But the realm is just black.
There aren't any colors.

535
00:41:11,958 --> 00:41:15,291
I thought you wouldn't want to practice
with the son of a thief

536
00:41:15,375 --> 00:41:17,125
who hurt you not once but twice.

537
00:41:17,208 --> 00:41:18,125
Whatever.

538
00:41:18,708 --> 00:41:23,500
One day, when you become a trance master,
I will be able to say,

539
00:41:23,583 --> 00:41:25,958
"He's a master thanks to me."

540
00:41:26,041 --> 00:41:27,041
Shut up.

541
00:41:31,250 --> 00:41:33,750
Do you prefer Jakarta or this place?

542
00:41:33,833 --> 00:41:35,625
I like it here, of course.

543
00:41:35,708 --> 00:41:38,666
My dad got scammed by his friend
in Jakarta.

544
00:41:39,333 --> 00:41:42,416
Dad lost everything.
Mom left him. We were starving.

545
00:41:43,250 --> 00:41:44,750
{\an8}Hey, that kind of rhymes.

546
00:41:44,833 --> 00:41:48,041
{\an8}Dad lost everything.
Mom left him. We were starving.

547
00:41:48,125 --> 00:41:49,458
And your head was spinning.

548
00:41:52,250 --> 00:41:56,458
{\an8}I had to drop out of vocational school.

549
00:41:57,250 --> 00:41:59,250
I did all kinds of odd jobs.

550
00:42:00,083 --> 00:42:01,083
Check it out.

551
00:42:03,083 --> 00:42:07,041
I did a gig as a silver human statue.

552
00:42:07,125 --> 00:42:10,583
I was a clown once.
I even begged for money.

553
00:42:10,666 --> 00:42:13,833
But when my dad got arrested,

554
00:42:13,916 --> 00:42:17,208
I came back here to live with my grandma.

555
00:42:18,000 --> 00:42:22,416
Then Pawit convinced me
to become a spirit host

556
00:42:22,500 --> 00:42:24,041
to get me out of my slump.

557
00:42:25,083 --> 00:42:27,250
The rest is history.

558
00:42:27,333 --> 00:42:29,666
I want to be a spirit channeler

559
00:42:29,750 --> 00:42:32,875
so that I can help people who are sad
feel better.

560
00:42:32,958 --> 00:42:33,958
Wow.

561
00:42:35,500 --> 00:42:36,458
Amazing.

562
00:42:36,541 --> 00:42:40,208
- My turn. I'll ask the questions now.
- What?

563
00:42:40,291 --> 00:42:43,125
I'll ask you some questions,
like Guru Asri did yesterday.

564
00:42:45,625 --> 00:42:46,833
I'm terrified.

565
00:42:47,708 --> 00:42:49,291
Where are you from?

566
00:42:49,375 --> 00:42:50,625
Jakarta.

567
00:42:50,708 --> 00:42:52,666
What did you do there?

568
00:42:52,750 --> 00:42:54,583
{\an8}I was an e-commerce employee.

569
00:42:55,583 --> 00:42:57,250
Why are you always barefoot?

570
00:42:58,041 --> 00:42:59,708
It's a fashion statement.

571
00:42:59,791 --> 00:43:02,000
Why did you come to Latas village?

572
00:43:02,083 --> 00:43:03,791
To build a hotel.

573
00:43:03,875 --> 00:43:05,916
{\an8}Liar, liar.

574
00:43:08,083 --> 00:43:09,375
{\an8}To heal.

575
00:43:09,458 --> 00:43:11,041
Heal from what?

576
00:43:14,125 --> 00:43:14,958
Trauma.

577
00:43:16,333 --> 00:43:17,791
What kind of trauma?

578
00:43:20,375 --> 00:43:22,083
I don't like these questions.

579
00:43:23,458 --> 00:43:24,958
No. I can't tell you that yet.

580
00:43:25,708 --> 00:43:27,208
Why not?

581
00:43:27,833 --> 00:43:31,166
Because my voucher expired,
and I got hit with a rattan stick.

582
00:43:31,250 --> 00:43:33,625
It hurt so much that it gave me amnesia.

583
00:43:34,500 --> 00:43:37,291
Yeah. Why was I so stupid?

584
00:43:38,708 --> 00:43:42,333
{\an8}But did you overcome the trauma?

585
00:43:43,125 --> 00:43:44,708
I've tried everything.

586
00:43:46,166 --> 00:43:48,041
Alcohol, meditation…

587
00:43:48,958 --> 00:43:52,166
I even got fancy and went to Bali.
Nothing worked.

588
00:43:53,708 --> 00:43:59,333
{\an8}Then my brother showed me a documentary
about trance parties and I was intrigued.

589
00:44:00,333 --> 00:44:03,458
{\an8}So I came here. I gave it a try.

590
00:44:04,125 --> 00:44:05,375
And I liked it.

591
00:44:06,583 --> 00:44:10,500
After a trance, I'm always relaxed.
Like after a yoga session.

592
00:44:11,166 --> 00:44:13,208
- Did you grow a mustache too?
- What?

593
00:44:13,916 --> 00:44:15,916
You mean if I became more masculine?

594
00:44:16,000 --> 00:44:19,083
I mean like my friend, Yoga.
A channeler at Bondan's school.

595
00:44:19,958 --> 00:44:21,500
{\an8}- What the…
- He has a moustache.

596
00:44:21,583 --> 00:44:23,000
{\an8}That's so lame.

597
00:44:23,083 --> 00:44:29,000
But he used to be barefoot
all the time as well.

598
00:44:29,083 --> 00:44:31,000
- You're lame.
- His feet became mouldy.

599
00:44:31,083 --> 00:44:34,125
I'm not joking.
I'd rub his feet clean every day.

600
00:44:34,208 --> 00:44:36,750
Why? Just bring him here.
This place is a fish spa.

601
00:44:36,833 --> 00:44:38,458
Fish spa? You're right.

602
00:44:40,333 --> 00:44:41,583
But you…

603
00:44:42,625 --> 00:44:44,208
Your brother's not here with you?

604
00:44:45,333 --> 00:44:47,750
No. He's far away.

605
00:44:51,166 --> 00:44:54,166
Hey, bring that raft back here!

606
00:44:54,250 --> 00:44:57,041
- We need to cross.
- Okay. I'm sorry.

607
00:44:58,250 --> 00:45:01,333
Good morning, people of Latas.

608
00:45:01,416 --> 00:45:02,958
Good morning!

609
00:45:03,041 --> 00:45:07,541
The Central School is conducting
a selection for our new spirit channeler.

610
00:45:07,625 --> 00:45:10,791
Only six candidates remain
from the initial group of eight.

611
00:45:10,875 --> 00:45:13,625
The spirit channeler
who gets selected today

612
00:45:13,708 --> 00:45:16,458
will perform at the big party
at the end of the month.

613
00:45:17,250 --> 00:45:22,625
Thank you, Mr. Budi and Mrs. Rina,
our hosts for Arif's circumcision party.

614
00:45:22,708 --> 00:45:26,333
They were kind enough
to hold a trance party for us.

615
00:45:27,458 --> 00:45:29,875
The hotel construction is just an excuse.

616
00:45:30,583 --> 00:45:36,208
Wanaria wants our spring for this!

617
00:45:36,958 --> 00:45:39,416
If that happens, we're doomed.

618
00:45:39,500 --> 00:45:42,000
There'll be no water left
for our rice fields.

619
00:45:42,083 --> 00:45:46,625
In the neighboring village,
everybody was forced to sell their land.

620
00:45:46,708 --> 00:45:49,166
Now they have
a miserable life in the city.

621
00:45:49,250 --> 00:45:52,708
- Latas is not for sale!
- Latas is not for sale!

622
00:45:53,875 --> 00:45:59,375
Wanaria Group is holding a music concert
to win people over.

623
00:45:59,458 --> 00:46:05,958
But we know better.
This is where the real party is!

624
00:46:06,041 --> 00:46:08,208
Yes!

625
00:46:08,291 --> 00:46:10,125
See the blackboard behind me?

626
00:46:10,208 --> 00:46:14,708
You all can vote here
for the best spirit channeler.

627
00:46:14,791 --> 00:46:21,125
Our first channeler is Ananto
and his powerful fire ant spirit!

628
00:46:21,208 --> 00:46:23,916
Eat, devour, enjoy!

629
00:46:38,833 --> 00:46:42,291
My mother married my father in Dubai.

630
00:46:42,375 --> 00:46:47,833
My father was a Dutch cook.
That's why I have a superior taste.

631
00:46:47,916 --> 00:46:53,791
Today, I'm going to treat you all
to some great food from around the world.

632
00:46:53,875 --> 00:46:58,500
But before that,
let's welcome our guest of honor.

633
00:46:58,583 --> 00:46:59,916
Arif!

634
00:47:19,458 --> 00:47:20,875
For our hors d'oeuvres,

635
00:47:21,666 --> 00:47:23,583
raw bamboo shoots!

636
00:47:28,291 --> 00:47:30,333
But thanks to the fire ant spirit,

637
00:47:31,791 --> 00:47:33,625
these bamboo shoots will taste like…

638
00:47:35,291 --> 00:47:36,833
croissants!

639
00:47:45,833 --> 00:47:47,208
Our appetizer!

640
00:47:49,125 --> 00:47:49,958
Sushi!

641
00:48:01,291 --> 00:48:02,291
Main course!

642
00:48:03,041 --> 00:48:04,375
Wagyu beef!

643
00:48:17,458 --> 00:48:18,333
And for dessert…

644
00:48:19,166 --> 00:48:21,583
Gelato!

645
00:48:34,666 --> 00:48:37,625
Where are the crackers?
We can't have a meal without crackers.

646
00:48:37,708 --> 00:48:41,083
You got it, my man! Get the plates out!

647
00:48:42,333 --> 00:48:44,708
Don't overdo it. You're not ready.

648
00:48:45,458 --> 00:48:46,583
Chill, ma'am.

649
00:48:47,375 --> 00:48:49,916
Coffee! One more black coffee!

650
00:48:50,000 --> 00:48:50,875
I got it.

651
00:48:52,083 --> 00:48:53,583
Coffee, please.

652
00:48:57,333 --> 00:48:59,583
- Not strong enough.
- Not strong enough?

653
00:49:10,500 --> 00:49:13,416
Here come the crackers!

654
00:49:13,500 --> 00:49:19,166
Crackling crackers crack!

655
00:49:36,333 --> 00:49:39,250
Shit, this coffee is so strong.

656
00:49:39,333 --> 00:49:42,291
Concentrate, don't lose them.

657
00:49:43,333 --> 00:49:45,041
If you hurt them, you're screwed.

658
00:49:45,125 --> 00:49:46,208
It's all right, ma'am.

659
00:50:10,000 --> 00:50:12,750
I told you not to be cocky.

660
00:50:12,833 --> 00:50:14,791
Look what happened.

661
00:50:14,875 --> 00:50:17,875
Learn your limits.
Your heart can't take it.

662
00:50:17,958 --> 00:50:19,208
Sorry, ma'am.

663
00:50:20,708 --> 00:50:22,208
Who wants to go next?

664
00:50:24,458 --> 00:50:25,666
Me.

665
00:50:27,208 --> 00:50:29,208
The turtle spirit?

666
00:50:29,875 --> 00:50:33,166
They're still bleeding and you
want to cane them with rattan sticks?

667
00:50:33,250 --> 00:50:35,208
I didn't bring the turtle this time.

668
00:50:36,208 --> 00:50:38,083
I just caught a new spirit.

669
00:50:40,625 --> 00:50:41,625
Bedbugs?

670
00:50:43,458 --> 00:50:44,333
Are you sure?

671
00:50:49,208 --> 00:50:51,958
A bedbug is about to bite!

672
00:50:52,041 --> 00:50:54,916
Rise and shine, look at it take flight!

673
00:51:13,208 --> 00:51:15,458
Bayu, bring in the spirit hosts!

674
00:51:19,375 --> 00:51:21,833
Bring in the bedbugs now!

675
00:52:11,625 --> 00:52:13,333
<i>Go back to being a human statue.</i>

676
00:52:14,916 --> 00:52:16,166
<i>Beg on the streets.</i>

677
00:52:17,250 --> 00:52:18,791
<i>Beg on the streets.</i>

678
00:52:32,458 --> 00:52:33,583
Do you need this?

679
00:52:34,208 --> 00:52:36,500
Guru Asri, the jumping mantra!

680
00:52:36,583 --> 00:52:38,541
What do you call a bedbug?

681
00:52:38,625 --> 00:52:41,583
The bouncing louse!

682
00:52:41,666 --> 00:52:45,833
The bouncing louse!

683
00:53:57,375 --> 00:53:59,416
This is only half of the money.

684
00:54:00,083 --> 00:54:04,166
We promise we'll pay you the rest soon.

685
00:54:04,958 --> 00:54:08,625
We also have a gift for you.

686
00:54:08,708 --> 00:54:12,583
A blanket for your grandson.
We hope he gets well soon.

687
00:54:12,666 --> 00:54:14,458
Thank you, ma'am.

688
00:54:15,166 --> 00:54:17,166
Thank you, everyone.

689
00:54:17,250 --> 00:54:18,833
Thank you, people of Latas.

690
00:54:22,458 --> 00:54:28,750
The party has gone viral on social media.
They're calling it the Trance Mania.

691
00:54:28,833 --> 00:54:32,333
Look at you jumping!
The bug princess from Jakarta.

692
00:54:33,416 --> 00:54:37,083
Wasn't your niece born three months ago?

693
00:54:37,583 --> 00:54:39,041
- Yes.
- She's a Leo, then.

694
00:54:39,125 --> 00:54:42,250
I'm not into zodiac signs.

695
00:54:42,333 --> 00:54:45,750
Leo is the lion. Find a lion.

696
00:54:45,833 --> 00:54:47,708
- A lion?
- It represents the Leo sign.

697
00:54:48,833 --> 00:54:50,791
Let's see. Do they even have a lion?

698
00:54:50,875 --> 00:54:52,375
I found a tiger.

699
00:54:53,583 --> 00:54:55,000
- That could work.
- Yeah.

700
00:54:55,083 --> 00:54:58,625
Hey, get her this color.
The same as her element.

701
00:54:58,708 --> 00:54:59,875
Get this one.

702
00:54:59,958 --> 00:55:01,500
What's her element?

703
00:55:01,583 --> 00:55:02,583
Fire, of course.

704
00:55:03,708 --> 00:55:05,916
What's your star sign?

705
00:55:06,000 --> 00:55:07,250
Guess.

706
00:55:10,250 --> 00:55:11,291
You're a movie star.

707
00:55:13,083 --> 00:55:14,208
You're so lame.

708
00:55:15,833 --> 00:55:17,625
- I'll give you a clue.
- Let's see.

709
00:55:17,708 --> 00:55:19,708
I was born in February.

710
00:55:20,833 --> 00:55:22,708
{\an8}- February.
- What is it?

711
00:55:23,333 --> 00:55:24,833
I told you I'm not into that.

712
00:55:24,916 --> 00:55:26,583
Look it up.

713
00:55:29,333 --> 00:55:32,166
{\an8}Hey, that's Mr. Banar.

714
00:55:32,958 --> 00:55:36,625
He's a former spirit channeler.
One of the greatest.

715
00:55:36,708 --> 00:55:38,000
Really?

716
00:55:38,083 --> 00:55:40,208
He's a legend. I'll be right back.

717
00:55:42,500 --> 00:55:43,833
- Mr. Banar.
- Hey.

718
00:55:43,916 --> 00:55:46,625
- Mr. Banar, I'm a big fan.
- Okay.

719
00:55:46,708 --> 00:55:49,375
- Can I take a selfie with you?
- Sure.

720
00:55:49,458 --> 00:55:50,458
Cool.

721
00:55:51,291 --> 00:55:54,416
- Your seahorse spirit was the best.
- You know that?

722
00:55:55,833 --> 00:55:57,833
One, two, three.

723
00:56:00,708 --> 00:56:02,458
It's raining! Thanks so much.

724
00:56:03,458 --> 00:56:04,333
Oh, boy.

725
00:56:06,708 --> 00:56:08,458
I'll take this one.

726
00:56:09,458 --> 00:56:11,000
- It's 20,000.
- 20,000?

727
00:56:11,083 --> 00:56:11,916
Yes.

728
00:56:14,083 --> 00:56:15,208
- Here you go.
- Okay.

729
00:56:16,125 --> 00:56:17,625
- Thank you.
- Yes.

730
00:56:18,333 --> 00:56:19,166
Laksmi?

731
00:56:21,708 --> 00:56:22,583
Laksmi?

732
00:56:25,458 --> 00:56:26,291
Laksmi?

733
00:56:29,291 --> 00:56:31,250
- Laksmi?
- Possess me.

734
00:56:31,333 --> 00:56:33,000
{\an8}- Possess me.
- Laksmi?

735
00:56:33,083 --> 00:56:34,333
It's raining.

736
00:56:41,958 --> 00:56:44,416
- Do you have essential oil, ma'am?
- Yes.

737
00:56:44,500 --> 00:56:45,458
- Thank you.
- Okay.

738
00:56:51,208 --> 00:56:52,833
Please possess me.

739
00:56:57,500 --> 00:56:59,750
I'm sorry.
I'm gonna touch your head, okay?

740
00:57:04,958 --> 00:57:06,875
I'll give you a head massage.

741
00:57:06,958 --> 00:57:09,958
We're in a public place,
so I can't put you in a trance.

742
00:57:11,333 --> 00:57:13,916
Lean back. You'll feel better.

743
00:57:20,958 --> 00:57:25,375
<i>I once asked my brother to give me</i>
<i>a ride downtown to buy running shoes.</i>

744
00:57:26,208 --> 00:57:32,041
<i>On the way, I kept telling him,</i>
<i>"Go faster. Hurry."</i>

745
00:57:33,708 --> 00:57:34,875
<i>So he sped up.</i>

746
00:57:36,708 --> 00:57:38,666
<i>Like a madman, in the rain.</i>

747
00:57:39,708 --> 00:57:41,291
<i>We got into an accident…</i>

748
00:57:43,958 --> 00:57:45,625
<i>and he died.</i>

749
00:57:47,708 --> 00:57:50,875
<i>Every time it rains,</i>
<i>I am reminded of my foolishness.</i>

750
00:57:51,833 --> 00:57:54,166
<i>I can't wear shoes anymore.</i>

751
00:57:55,458 --> 00:57:57,791
<i>Can you help me go into a trance, Bayu?</i>

752
00:57:59,333 --> 00:58:01,416
<i>I can't stand it when it rains.</i>

753
00:58:34,083 --> 00:58:35,083
Hello.

754
00:58:43,250 --> 00:58:44,958
- How are you?
- I'm good.

755
00:58:45,833 --> 00:58:48,916
- I got her a present.
- Thank you.

756
00:58:49,000 --> 00:58:50,958
- You're welcome.
- How long was the trip?

757
00:58:51,041 --> 00:58:53,125
- About two hours.
- Where do I put this?

758
00:58:53,208 --> 00:58:54,500
Over there.

759
00:58:54,583 --> 00:58:59,958
Yono, our neighbor in Latas
just moved to Jakarta.

760
00:59:00,041 --> 00:59:03,750
- Yeah.
- I heard Wanaria paid him a lot of money.

761
00:59:04,458 --> 00:59:08,041
Did they make an offer on Mom's house too?

762
00:59:11,958 --> 00:59:12,833
They did.

763
00:59:15,000 --> 00:59:16,625
250 million rupiah.

764
00:59:16,708 --> 00:59:20,875
What? That's a good offer.
Why didn't you tell me anything?

765
00:59:20,958 --> 00:59:21,958
It's not that.

766
00:59:22,583 --> 00:59:26,583
We were just negotiating.

767
00:59:26,666 --> 00:59:29,166
Try to get 350 if you can.

768
00:59:29,958 --> 00:59:31,000
I'll give it a try.

769
00:59:31,083 --> 00:59:33,750
That's a good number to split into three.

770
00:59:34,458 --> 00:59:37,625
One hundred for me, 100 for you,
and 100 for Wati.

771
00:59:38,208 --> 00:59:41,500
You can use the rest of the money
to start a business here.

772
00:59:41,583 --> 00:59:45,125
A friend of mine called Nana

773
00:59:45,208 --> 00:59:48,333
asked me to start
a water-dispenser business with her.

774
00:59:49,208 --> 00:59:51,583
Why don't you two just get married?

775
00:59:51,666 --> 00:59:55,625
It's convenient.
Bayu can help you with the deliveries.

776
00:59:55,708 --> 00:59:57,750
- That's not what I want.
- What?

777
00:59:58,333 --> 01:00:02,458
I don't want you to sell the house.
I like living in Latas.

778
01:00:02,541 --> 01:00:05,625
- How are you gonna earn a living there?
- Spirit-channeling.

779
01:00:05,708 --> 01:00:08,875
I just got selected
by the best trance school in the village.

780
01:00:08,958 --> 01:00:10,833
You still believe in that stuff?

781
01:00:10,916 --> 01:00:14,416
People acting like tigers and shit,
isn't that just a scam?

782
01:00:14,500 --> 01:00:17,333
Isn't there
a scientific explanation for that?

783
01:00:17,416 --> 01:00:20,083
Like when you can't move your body
in your sleep?

784
01:00:20,166 --> 01:00:21,875
Sleep paralysis.

785
01:00:21,958 --> 01:00:23,666
More like "sleep paragliding."

786
01:00:23,750 --> 01:00:26,875
That's why you have your head
in the clouds.

787
01:00:26,958 --> 01:00:27,875
Bullshit.

788
01:00:27,958 --> 01:00:29,166
- Bullshit.
- Bullshit.

789
01:00:30,041 --> 01:00:35,333
Uncle Rahmat, Aunt Wati and Dad
used to go to trance parties all the time.

790
01:00:35,416 --> 01:00:37,541
Just ask them.

791
01:00:37,625 --> 01:00:39,958
What was your spirit, Dad? A frog?

792
01:00:40,833 --> 01:00:42,083
A frog, that's funny.

793
01:00:42,166 --> 01:00:45,750
That was when I was in grade school
and junior high.

794
01:00:45,833 --> 01:00:47,166
I stopped after that.

795
01:00:47,250 --> 01:00:53,041
But many of my friends are still doing it
even though they're old now.

796
01:00:54,250 --> 01:00:56,666
It's not pretty.
Their lives are going nowhere.

797
01:00:56,750 --> 01:01:02,625
Mr. Banar lives a good life now.
He has a nice car and a fancy phone.

798
01:01:03,333 --> 01:01:07,208
Mr. Banar is not married.
You want to stay single your whole life?

799
01:01:07,791 --> 01:01:10,916
But I ran into him
and his girlfriend yesterday.

800
01:01:11,000 --> 01:01:13,291
But everyone in Latas
already sold their land.

801
01:01:13,375 --> 01:01:15,875
Who will you put in a trance?
The bulldozers?

802
01:01:15,958 --> 01:01:19,000
Tell them what you just got, son.

803
01:01:19,083 --> 01:01:20,250
- A promotion.
- Yes.

804
01:01:20,333 --> 01:01:22,458
See? You two are the same age, Bayu.

805
01:01:23,208 --> 01:01:25,708
He has saved up
to get married and buy a house.

806
01:01:25,791 --> 01:01:26,916
Next year.

807
01:01:28,083 --> 01:01:32,666
- Are you planning to stay single forever?
- Whatever. I chose a different life.

808
01:01:32,750 --> 01:01:35,291
Work is not all about marriage
and having children.

809
01:01:35,375 --> 01:01:36,416
What do you mean?

810
01:01:36,500 --> 01:01:43,458
I choose to do a job that can help people
and not just to fill up my own belly.

811
01:01:43,541 --> 01:01:45,708
You're saying my job doesn't help people?

812
01:01:45,791 --> 01:01:49,375
Just wait ten years.
See who gives more to charity.

813
01:01:49,458 --> 01:01:51,125
- I didn't say that.
- You did.

814
01:01:51,208 --> 01:01:54,083
What if in ten years
no one goes to those parties anymore?

815
01:01:54,166 --> 01:01:56,458
You'll just be a burden
because you'd be jobless.

816
01:01:56,541 --> 01:02:00,125
What I mean is,
people lead different lives.

817
01:02:00,208 --> 01:02:02,041
Different things make them happy.

818
01:02:02,125 --> 01:02:04,541
I've never burdened you,
so quit criticizing me.

819
01:02:04,625 --> 01:02:06,250
You're living off my dad's money.

820
01:02:06,333 --> 01:02:07,625
Then keep your money.

821
01:02:07,708 --> 01:02:11,750
Enough! What's with the yelling?
You're too loud.

822
01:02:11,833 --> 01:02:14,291
You always fight
whenever you see each other.

823
01:02:19,208 --> 01:02:20,875
Watch that attitude.

824
01:02:21,833 --> 01:02:24,958
Bayu, you shouldn't be like that
with our family.

825
01:02:25,583 --> 01:02:26,541
It's not nice.

826
01:02:27,208 --> 01:02:30,375
Why did you tell them?
You promised you wouldn't.

827
01:02:30,458 --> 01:02:34,458
The house isn't mine alone.
We've talked about this.

828
01:02:36,208 --> 01:02:38,875
I told you I'd pay for the house
in installments.

829
01:02:38,958 --> 01:02:41,583
I got into the top four.
Just one more stage.

830
01:02:41,666 --> 01:02:45,791
But there's no guarantee.
It'll take you forever to get the money.

831
01:02:45,875 --> 01:02:47,958
Better to get the money slowly but surely,

832
01:02:48,041 --> 01:02:52,375
than have you start a business
with Mrs. Nana and fail.

833
01:02:52,458 --> 01:02:55,000
The debt collectors
will be on our asses again.

834
01:02:55,083 --> 01:02:58,125
It's only been a day
and this city's already suffocating me.

835
01:02:58,833 --> 01:03:01,333
Bayu!

836
01:03:02,583 --> 01:03:06,500
Sorry about earlier.
I didn't mean to piss you off.

837
01:03:06,583 --> 01:03:10,958
I got carried away.
We're going out to chill. Come join us!

838
01:03:12,000 --> 01:03:14,291
No, thanks. I have to get back tonight.

839
01:03:14,375 --> 01:03:18,000
What a party pooper!
Come on, just this once.

840
01:03:18,083 --> 01:03:19,958
- Join us, Bayu!
- Come on!

841
01:03:20,041 --> 01:03:21,500
Just go with them.

842
01:03:21,583 --> 01:03:27,708
Humor them for once. They're family.
Uncle Rahmat has been so nice to us.

843
01:03:27,791 --> 01:03:29,250
Hurry! We'll wait for you.

844
01:03:29,333 --> 01:03:30,708
- Let's go!
- Come on!

845
01:03:40,625 --> 01:03:44,041
Hey! Why are you so quiet?

846
01:03:45,708 --> 01:03:48,833
Let's hit the floor.

847
01:03:49,958 --> 01:03:50,916
I don't dance.

848
01:03:51,000 --> 01:03:52,791
- What?
- I don't do this stuff.

849
01:03:52,875 --> 01:03:54,416
You don't?

850
01:03:54,500 --> 01:03:58,000
- Let me teach you some moves.
- Yeah. Show him!

851
01:04:00,583 --> 01:04:02,333
Damn!

852
01:04:02,416 --> 01:04:04,916
Drink up. It'll get you in the mood.

853
01:04:05,000 --> 01:04:07,458
No, I don't drink this stuff.

854
01:04:08,833 --> 01:04:10,875
He only gets drunk with cows.

855
01:04:10,958 --> 01:04:13,083
Don't force him.

856
01:04:13,166 --> 01:04:15,083
He prefers ritual offerings.

857
01:04:16,708 --> 01:04:19,750
I bet this is how he parties
back in his village.

858
01:04:19,833 --> 01:04:20,666
How?

859
01:04:21,208 --> 01:04:22,500
Oh, shit!

860
01:04:22,583 --> 01:04:24,125
Bull, bull!

861
01:04:26,083 --> 01:04:27,958
My turn.

862
01:04:29,208 --> 01:04:31,666
- So? What am I?
- A tiger!

863
01:05:41,208 --> 01:05:43,333
Well? Was it good?

864
01:05:44,750 --> 01:05:47,375
Yeah, it was good.

865
01:05:47,458 --> 01:05:50,125
Look at Spiderman here, all lovey-dovey.

866
01:05:52,333 --> 01:05:53,416
You're heavy, asshole.

867
01:05:55,333 --> 01:05:56,625
Sorry, dude.

868
01:06:01,708 --> 01:06:06,208
Not bad, but not as good as yesterday.

869
01:06:07,333 --> 01:06:10,500
- What was on your mind?
- My relatives in Jakarta.

870
01:06:11,583 --> 01:06:12,416
And?

871
01:06:13,125 --> 01:06:17,000
They were making fun of what we do here.

872
01:06:18,083 --> 01:06:19,916
They tried to make me drink.

873
01:06:20,000 --> 01:06:23,458
And my uncle is trying to convince my dad
to sell the house.

874
01:06:24,083 --> 01:06:27,541
By the way, while you were
getting drunk in Jakarta--

875
01:06:27,625 --> 01:06:29,250
I didn't get drunk, ma'am!

876
01:06:29,333 --> 01:06:32,000
The villagers proposed
a new spirit channeler.

877
01:06:33,208 --> 01:06:35,541
- Hey, kid!
- Yes, ma'am!

878
01:06:35,625 --> 01:06:37,041
- Come here.
- Excuse me.

879
01:06:40,125 --> 01:06:41,125
Yes.

880
01:06:41,208 --> 01:06:43,333
My man!

881
01:06:43,416 --> 01:06:48,541
Get ready, you're up after Bayu.
The villagers want to see what you've got.

882
01:06:49,333 --> 01:06:51,291
- What's your spirit?
- This, ma'am.

883
01:06:53,000 --> 01:06:55,958
Whoa, okay. Get ready.

884
01:07:06,958 --> 01:07:09,958
Ma'am, this isn't fair.

885
01:07:10,916 --> 01:07:15,333
He wasn't even in the selection process,
and now he's leading the trance party?

886
01:07:16,083 --> 01:07:19,458
- The other guys won't be happy either.
- Not happy?

887
01:07:19,541 --> 01:07:22,250
That's what the villagers want.
What can I do?

888
01:07:22,333 --> 01:07:25,625
Maybe he's been fasting
more than the others.

889
01:07:25,708 --> 01:07:26,833
We'll see.

890
01:07:27,958 --> 01:07:29,583
- Excuse me.
- Yes.

891
01:07:32,833 --> 01:07:35,583
A drought affects Latas.
Let's bathe in the spirit realm.

892
01:07:35,666 --> 01:07:38,041
Buffaloes locking their horns!

893
01:07:38,125 --> 01:07:40,916
Drenched in rose-infused water
without thorns!

894
01:07:54,458 --> 01:07:55,750
Soap!

895
01:07:55,833 --> 01:07:57,375
Wash yourselves with soap!

896
01:08:11,916 --> 01:08:13,083
Wash your hair!

897
01:08:13,166 --> 01:08:15,000
Time to wash your hair!

898
01:08:29,625 --> 01:08:31,250
Brush your teeth!

899
01:08:42,750 --> 01:08:44,375
Dry yourselves!

900
01:08:51,541 --> 01:08:52,500
Spray some cologne!

901
01:09:10,208 --> 01:09:11,583
- Amazing!
- Careful.

902
01:09:12,708 --> 01:09:16,375
Your trance effect is the best one so far.
So refreshing.

903
01:09:16,458 --> 01:09:17,333
Not bad.

904
01:09:18,375 --> 01:09:19,458
That was good!

905
01:09:21,583 --> 01:09:24,750
Judges, we'll add Pawit's name
on the board.

906
01:09:26,208 --> 01:09:30,416
Doni, Yuli, thanks for taking part
in this selection process.

907
01:09:30,500 --> 01:09:32,250
All the best.

908
01:09:32,333 --> 01:09:33,166
- Ma'am.
- Thanks.

909
01:09:33,250 --> 01:09:36,000
Ma'am, you can't just do
whatever you want.

910
01:09:36,958 --> 01:09:38,333
Whatever I want?

911
01:09:39,791 --> 01:09:41,708
What we want

912
01:09:42,583 --> 01:09:45,625
is for the villagers
to enjoy their lives in Latas.

913
01:09:45,708 --> 01:09:48,166
So they're not forced
to sell their land to Wanaria.

914
01:09:48,250 --> 01:09:50,250
We need the best spirit channeler.

915
01:09:50,333 --> 01:09:53,250
If you can't get your mind off
your cousins in Jakarta,

916
01:09:53,333 --> 01:09:55,291
maybe you should join them there.

917
01:09:55,375 --> 01:09:56,875
Forget about being a channeler.

918
01:09:56,958 --> 01:10:00,750
But if you think you're better
than the others, then prove it.

919
01:10:00,833 --> 01:10:05,208
Get an upper-rank spirit for the final.

920
01:10:09,208 --> 01:10:10,333
Horse.

921
01:10:11,833 --> 01:10:12,833
Tiger.

922
01:10:14,833 --> 01:10:15,666
Leech.

923
01:10:30,458 --> 01:10:33,833
<i>Bayu, I'm selling the house to Fahri.</i>
<i>Is that okay?</i>

924
01:10:34,708 --> 01:10:37,625
<i>Come on, move to the city.</i>
<i>Trust me, it's the best.</i>

925
01:10:37,708 --> 01:10:42,750
<i>If I get scammed again, we'll starve.</i>
<i>I'll need to steal another phone.</i>

926
01:10:42,833 --> 01:10:45,125
<i>You can put the phone owner in a trance.</i>

927
01:10:46,000 --> 01:10:51,875
<i>If they beat me up, put me in a trance.</i>
<i>Use the turtle spirit so I'm protected.</i>

928
01:10:51,958 --> 01:10:55,125
<i>They're hitting your dad,</i>
<i>but it feels like a gentle massage.</i>

929
01:10:55,208 --> 01:10:56,208
I'm a tiger.

930
01:10:57,833 --> 01:11:02,583
<i>If I go to jail, you won't starve.</i>
<i>You're used to fasting.</i>

931
01:11:03,583 --> 01:11:08,291
<i>In the city, you can get</i>
<i>the highest-ranked spirit. The cockroach.</i>

932
01:11:08,958 --> 01:11:09,833
I'm a leech.

933
01:11:46,583 --> 01:11:48,583
You got the snake!

934
01:11:51,083 --> 01:11:52,500
I'm kidding.

935
01:11:52,583 --> 01:11:55,833
Hey, trance master,
what spirit are you trying to catch?

936
01:11:56,708 --> 01:11:59,125
The worm? The caterpillar?

937
01:12:01,000 --> 01:12:06,750
I see. You're not talking because
you're getting ready for the final, huh?

938
01:12:06,833 --> 01:12:13,208
{\an8}Guru Asri asked me to make
a new costume for the big party.

939
01:12:14,291 --> 01:12:19,625
I'm her apprentice now.
You told me not to work for Wanaria.

940
01:12:19,708 --> 01:12:21,250
{\an8}Let me take your measurements.

941
01:12:21,333 --> 01:12:23,625
{\an8}Now's a good time.
You're in the right position.

942
01:12:23,708 --> 01:12:28,583
Hey, why haven't you asked me
to practice with you again?

943
01:12:29,583 --> 01:12:30,958
I miss it.

944
01:12:33,208 --> 01:12:35,625
I miss going into a trance.

945
01:12:37,708 --> 01:12:38,833
Want to do it later?

946
01:12:39,875 --> 01:12:41,500
I brought you some chicken soup.

947
01:12:43,500 --> 01:12:45,333
<i>Bring Laksmi some chicken soup.</i>

948
01:12:46,083 --> 01:12:48,625
<i>Guru Asri will choose Pawit</i>
<i>as the spirit channeler.</i>

949
01:12:48,708 --> 01:12:52,208
<i>Laksmi will fall in love with Pawit</i>
<i>and marry him.</i>

950
01:12:53,000 --> 01:12:56,875
<i>Laksmi and Pawit will have a child</i>
<i>and I'll be all alone.</i>

951
01:12:56,958 --> 01:13:00,750
<i>They'll forget about me</i>
<i>and I'll be all alone until I'm old.</i>

952
01:13:00,833 --> 01:13:03,333
<i>I'll die and they'll find me</i>
<i>after three days.</i>

953
01:13:08,708 --> 01:13:10,250
"With…"

954
01:13:10,333 --> 01:13:11,833
"With Pawit," what?

955
01:13:12,625 --> 01:13:15,208
But you're my practice partner.
So it has to be you.

956
01:13:15,291 --> 01:13:17,208
A leech doesn't speak or eat.

957
01:13:17,291 --> 01:13:20,125
A leech doesn't speak? But you just spoke.

958
01:13:20,208 --> 01:13:23,083
What's with you? Did I do something wrong?

959
01:14:21,875 --> 01:14:25,000
This is not fair to my student's family.

960
01:14:25,083 --> 01:14:28,916
Sorry, ma'am, but I told you many times.
I have the deeds with me.

961
01:14:29,000 --> 01:14:32,083
I have bought all these properties
through a realtor.

962
01:14:32,166 --> 01:14:35,375
Where is this person?
I told you to bring him here.

963
01:14:35,458 --> 01:14:39,875
The previous owner and my mom agreed
that this land would be a green space.

964
01:14:39,958 --> 01:14:41,458
Why do you want to build here?

965
01:14:41,541 --> 01:14:45,125
If this turns into housing,
all the rice fields will be gone!

966
01:14:45,208 --> 01:14:47,500
Can you show me the written agreement?

967
01:14:47,583 --> 01:14:49,500
His mother is a migrant worker in Qatar.

968
01:14:49,583 --> 01:14:51,250
We can call her to discuss--

969
01:14:51,333 --> 01:14:56,125
Do you know what time it is there?
It's 4:00 a.m. My mother's asleep!

970
01:14:56,208 --> 01:14:59,916
Sure she's asleep? She could just be
coming back from her "job."

971
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:02,416
- Calm down!
- Eat shit!

972
01:15:02,500 --> 01:15:05,333
Come here!

973
01:15:10,458 --> 01:15:11,291
Bayu.

974
01:15:12,458 --> 01:15:14,541
Bayu, we need help here.

975
01:15:14,625 --> 01:15:17,833
Stop that.
They're trying to buy Ananto's rice field.

976
01:15:18,583 --> 01:15:21,833
Tell them what Wanaria plans to do.
What did they say?

977
01:15:21,916 --> 01:15:24,750
What's with you lately? Say something.

978
01:15:24,833 --> 01:15:25,916
Bayu!

979
01:15:30,291 --> 01:15:34,750
"I'm a leech. I'm a spirit channeler.
If Pawit wins, I'll sell my house."

980
01:15:34,833 --> 01:15:37,125
"If Ananto wins, I'll go back to Jakarta."

981
01:15:37,208 --> 01:15:40,375
"Laksmi's a distraction. I'm a leech.
If I win, I keep my home."

982
01:15:41,208 --> 01:15:42,458
Are you mad?

983
01:15:42,541 --> 01:15:46,125
Just because I'm now in the race
to become a spirit channeler?

984
01:15:46,208 --> 01:15:49,833
That was up to Guru Asri.
I had nothing to do with it.

985
01:15:49,916 --> 01:15:52,833
If you don't help us,
none of us will be spirit channelers.

986
01:16:15,125 --> 01:16:17,125
Let me tend to your wounds.

987
01:16:18,000 --> 01:16:20,500
Then we'll go practice,
I'll come with you.

988
01:16:32,500 --> 01:16:35,000
Holy crap.

989
01:16:36,875 --> 01:16:39,250
Does it have to be like this?

990
01:16:41,500 --> 01:16:42,500
I know.

991
01:16:43,666 --> 01:16:48,041
You're mad because I liked
Pawit's buffalo spirit, right?

992
01:16:50,125 --> 01:16:52,708
That doesn't mean
your bedbug spirit is not good.

993
01:16:52,791 --> 01:16:55,916
You said you wanted to become
a spirit channeler

994
01:16:56,000 --> 01:16:57,916
because you love seeing people happy.

995
01:16:58,000 --> 01:17:00,375
{\an8}How can we be happy to see you like this?

996
01:17:02,375 --> 01:17:05,000
The point of a trance party
is to have fun.

997
01:17:05,083 --> 01:17:06,875
Not to torture yourself like this.

998
01:18:13,666 --> 01:18:14,541
Bayu?

999
01:18:19,500 --> 01:18:20,666
Bayu?

1000
01:18:20,750 --> 01:18:23,750
I am not going back to Jakarta.

1001
01:18:23,833 --> 01:18:25,375
Hear me out first.

1002
01:18:25,458 --> 01:18:28,583
I don't want to go back
to eating once every two days.

1003
01:18:29,708 --> 01:18:32,250
Uncle Rahmat and Aunt Wati have agreed.

1004
01:18:33,625 --> 01:18:38,125
I'm sick and tired
of all your businesses that go nowhere.

1005
01:18:39,250 --> 01:18:41,750
I wanted to tell you,
but you were gone for a week.

1006
01:18:44,416 --> 01:18:47,333
- Bayu?
- Mom left because of you!

1007
01:18:48,958 --> 01:18:51,833
I will put an end to all our misfortunes.

1008
01:19:08,041 --> 01:19:12,125
I apologize for not being
like other fathers.

1009
01:19:12,916 --> 01:19:15,041
I'm a failure.

1010
01:19:15,125 --> 01:19:18,250
That's why I'm not trying
to get in the way of your work here.

1011
01:19:19,000 --> 01:19:20,541
This house has been sold.

1012
01:19:21,375 --> 01:19:23,375
But I convinced your Uncle Rahmat…

1013
01:19:26,041 --> 01:19:27,750
not to sell the shed.

1014
01:19:28,791 --> 01:19:30,541
You can still live here.

1015
01:19:32,041 --> 01:19:34,041
You've already got what you wanted.

1016
01:19:37,875 --> 01:19:38,875
But I haven't.

1017
01:19:41,250 --> 01:19:43,125
Let me give it another try.

1018
01:20:10,041 --> 01:20:11,250
Don't disappear.

1019
01:20:12,000 --> 01:20:13,541
Don't disappear.

1020
01:20:13,625 --> 01:20:16,250
{\an8}I'm a leech, I'm a leech.

1021
01:20:17,000 --> 01:20:18,541
{\an8}Don't disappear.

1022
01:21:15,625 --> 01:21:17,500
A tiger crouching next to a strait!

1023
01:21:17,583 --> 01:21:20,416
Don't throw anyone as bait!

1024
01:21:38,500 --> 01:21:39,666
The rooster spirit.

1025
01:21:39,750 --> 01:21:41,500
The rooster defies death!

1026
01:21:41,583 --> 01:21:44,291
Until its very last breath!

1027
01:22:04,250 --> 01:22:05,791
The leech spirit.

1028
01:22:05,875 --> 01:22:07,750
Leeches of the forest survive!

1029
01:22:07,833 --> 01:22:10,708
Let's eat them alive!

1030
01:22:24,000 --> 01:22:28,291
<i>The leech spirit will suck the blood</i>
<i>of all those who have hurt you.</i>

1031
01:22:28,375 --> 01:22:31,666
<i>Your father, your friend,</i>
<i>your significant other, your cousins.</i>

1032
01:22:31,750 --> 01:22:34,083
<i>Their blood will be drained</i>
<i>by the leech spirit!</i>

1033
01:22:36,416 --> 01:22:39,166
<i>Those who have provoked</i>
<i>inheritance disputes,</i>

1034
01:22:39,250 --> 01:22:41,208
<i>the leech will suck them dry.</i>

1035
01:22:42,500 --> 01:22:47,000
<i>Those childhood friends who hurt you,</i>
<i>the leech will eat them alive.</i>

1036
01:22:55,333 --> 01:23:00,541
<i>Neighbors, unfaithful partners,</i>
<i>scammers, thieves,</i>

1037
01:23:00,625 --> 01:23:03,000
<i>the leech will suck them dry.</i>

1038
01:23:07,833 --> 01:23:10,708
<i>The world will be a better place</i>
<i>without bad people.</i>

1039
01:23:10,791 --> 01:23:14,541
<i>The world will be a better place</i>
<i>if only good people remain!</i>

1040
01:23:14,625 --> 01:23:19,041
<i>The world will be a better place</i>
<i>if people don't hurt each other!</i>

1041
01:23:22,958 --> 01:23:27,250
<i>The leech will wipe them out!</i>

1042
01:23:37,000 --> 01:23:39,000
Let's hear the final score.

1043
01:23:43,541 --> 01:23:44,375
Bayu.

1044
01:23:48,666 --> 01:23:49,791
Ananto.

1045
01:23:53,666 --> 01:23:54,500
Bayu.

1046
01:23:58,750 --> 01:23:59,625
Ananto.

1047
01:24:03,875 --> 01:24:05,791
And the final vote…

1048
01:24:14,250 --> 01:24:15,125
Ananto.

1049
01:24:16,500 --> 01:24:17,458
The results are in.

1050
01:24:17,541 --> 01:24:21,541
Bayu, two votes. Pawit, no votes.
Ananto, three votes.

1051
01:24:21,625 --> 01:24:25,333
We have a new spirit channeler.
Ananto Prasetya!

1052
01:24:25,416 --> 01:24:32,416
<i>Even if it's hot like a boiling pot</i>

1053
01:24:33,625 --> 01:24:40,166
<i>Our prosperous Latas never disappoints</i>

1054
01:24:40,875 --> 01:24:47,875
<i>Our fields are yellow, full of worms</i>

1055
01:24:48,875 --> 01:24:51,291
<i>Our goats are healthy…</i>

1056
01:24:51,375 --> 01:24:55,291
We haven't seen a leech spirit like yours
in 20 years.

1057
01:24:57,125 --> 01:24:59,666
We're very impressed
that you can channel it.

1058
01:25:01,166 --> 01:25:04,791
But it didn't make us happy.

1059
01:25:06,000 --> 01:25:10,291
Instead, it made us
want to kill the people we hate.

1060
01:25:12,250 --> 01:25:14,125
It wouldn't be right for this village.

1061
01:25:37,125 --> 01:25:41,291
{\an8}PROPERTY OF WANARIA LLC
NO TRESPASSING

1062
01:26:11,000 --> 01:26:12,333
What spirit is it now?

1063
01:26:16,166 --> 01:26:17,541
Can I do it too?

1064
01:26:22,291 --> 01:26:23,791
I'm exhausted, too.

1065
01:26:28,166 --> 01:26:31,000
I know how you feel.

1066
01:26:40,250 --> 01:26:41,625
{\an8}Abandoned by your father.

1067
01:26:45,000 --> 01:26:46,541
{\an8}Being taken for granted.

1068
01:27:10,375 --> 01:27:14,583
Mr. Banar,
I failed to become a spirit channeler

1069
01:27:14,666 --> 01:27:17,250
because my father hurt me.

1070
01:27:17,333 --> 01:27:19,333
Calm down, Bayu.

1071
01:27:19,416 --> 01:27:22,166
To be a spirit channeler,
you have to have a big heart,

1072
01:27:23,000 --> 01:27:27,791
because our share of happiness
is meant for others.

1073
01:27:27,875 --> 01:27:31,000
I've fasted. I smell like an animal.

1074
01:27:31,083 --> 01:27:33,125
Just to be like you.

1075
01:27:33,208 --> 01:27:36,541
I don't mind
not having a wife or a family.

1076
01:27:36,625 --> 01:27:39,958
No family? Do you hear yourself?

1077
01:27:40,875 --> 01:27:46,208
All this time, haven't you ever wondered
why I always wear a jacket?

1078
01:27:46,916 --> 01:27:49,750
I'm thin as a skeleton,
but my belly weighs a ton.

1079
01:27:49,833 --> 01:27:51,625
You know about seahorses, right?

1080
01:27:54,083 --> 01:27:59,875
Female seahorses deposit their eggs
into the male's abdomen.

1081
01:28:06,625 --> 01:28:07,541
Sir.

1082
01:28:12,916 --> 01:28:14,083
Sir, don't.

1083
01:28:17,875 --> 01:28:21,875
If you failed yesterday, that means
you didn't really embody the spirit.

1084
01:28:23,375 --> 01:28:27,041
It's the male seahorses
that carry the babies.

1085
01:28:28,125 --> 01:28:29,750
I had to become a seahorse.

1086
01:28:31,000 --> 01:28:33,875
You think I don't have children?

1087
01:28:36,125 --> 01:28:40,500
This is my child.
It's been safe and sound inside my belly.

1088
01:28:40,583 --> 01:28:45,125
Everything has a price,
and that includes our own family.

1089
01:28:51,750 --> 01:28:52,583
Bayu.

1090
01:28:53,375 --> 01:28:57,166
I know your mind is foggy right now,
but I need your help.

1091
01:28:58,250 --> 01:29:00,750
Can you please put me in a trance?

1092
01:29:02,208 --> 01:29:03,625
It's raining.

1093
01:29:04,333 --> 01:29:06,291
You know how I get when it rains.

1094
01:29:08,000 --> 01:29:09,666
You can use this as your practice.

1095
01:29:10,750 --> 01:29:14,416
You gave this to me, remember?
Free trance anytime.

1096
01:29:17,416 --> 01:29:19,416
{\an8}I need it now, Bayu.

1097
01:29:19,500 --> 01:29:24,666
I know. You have to suck my blood
like a leech now, right?

1098
01:29:31,416 --> 01:29:32,958
Drink my blood.

1099
01:29:42,750 --> 01:29:46,000
Fine. If you don't wanna help me,
I'll go into a trance myself.

1100
01:29:47,000 --> 01:29:51,250
<i>- Leeches of the forest survive!</i>
<i>- Let's eat them alive!</i>

1101
01:30:56,750 --> 01:30:57,583
Laksmi?

1102
01:31:03,625 --> 01:31:04,500
Laksmi!

1103
01:31:05,541 --> 01:31:07,000
Laksmi!

1104
01:31:10,125 --> 01:31:11,250
Laksmi!

1105
01:31:14,250 --> 01:31:15,541
- Help!
- Laksmi!

1106
01:31:15,625 --> 01:31:19,583
- Something has attacked the chicken farm!
- Laksmi!

1107
01:31:19,666 --> 01:31:20,750
Laksmi!

1108
01:31:37,083 --> 01:31:37,958
Laksmi!

1109
01:31:39,458 --> 01:31:40,291
Laksmi!

1110
01:31:41,250 --> 01:31:42,250
Laksmi!

1111
01:31:50,625 --> 01:31:51,666
Laksmi!

1112
01:32:00,750 --> 01:32:01,583
Laksmi!

1113
01:32:02,666 --> 01:32:03,500
Laksmi.

1114
01:32:29,375 --> 01:32:30,208
Laksmi!

1115
01:32:50,000 --> 01:32:51,916
Laksmi.

1116
01:32:56,500 --> 01:32:59,000
Snap out of it, Laksmi.

1117
01:33:00,000 --> 01:33:02,500
I'll be there for you from now on.

1118
01:33:03,875 --> 01:33:04,708
Laksmi.

1119
01:33:34,041 --> 01:33:35,083
Now, Bayu!

1120
01:34:00,833 --> 01:34:02,000
Why are you so stubborn?

1121
01:34:03,416 --> 01:34:05,083
Still want to do everything alone?

1122
01:34:05,666 --> 01:34:07,375
It could kill her, you know that?

1123
01:34:20,333 --> 01:34:24,250
<i>We found who slaughtered the chickens.</i>
<i>All units on site.</i>

1124
01:34:34,791 --> 01:34:36,791
This is the second time, ma'am.

1125
01:34:38,416 --> 01:34:39,916
We did nothing wrong.

1126
01:34:41,250 --> 01:34:43,750
But your people keep on terrorizing us.

1127
01:34:44,500 --> 01:34:46,666
Calm down, let me explain…

1128
01:34:46,750 --> 01:34:49,458
Explain what? Look at this.

1129
01:34:50,750 --> 01:34:52,541
- Look.
- Okay, okay.

1130
01:34:52,625 --> 01:34:54,875
- We understand.
- We can see it.

1131
01:34:54,958 --> 01:34:56,291
We have eyes. Back off.

1132
01:34:59,625 --> 01:35:02,875
I talked to the Wanaria representatives.

1133
01:35:04,125 --> 01:35:08,333
They lost about 20 million rupiah
because of what happened.

1134
01:35:10,000 --> 01:35:11,291
Can you pay for it?

1135
01:35:12,250 --> 01:35:14,958
I can.
I'm sorry for all the trouble I caused.

1136
01:35:15,041 --> 01:35:15,875
It's fine.

1137
01:35:17,250 --> 01:35:19,375
You can stay here and rest.

1138
01:35:22,375 --> 01:35:23,500
And as for you, Bayu…

1139
01:35:25,625 --> 01:35:27,625
A butterfly perches on a horn.

1140
01:35:29,000 --> 01:35:31,833
You try to catch it, and it flies away.

1141
01:35:35,000 --> 01:35:36,875
You search for gold until you're torn.

1142
01:35:38,750 --> 01:35:40,166
Once it's in your hands…

1143
01:35:42,125 --> 01:35:43,708
your loved ones slip away.

1144
01:36:00,750 --> 01:36:03,125
I shouldn't have forced you
to redeem my voucher.

1145
01:36:07,541 --> 01:36:11,041
Come to think of it,
my brother died because of a voucher.

1146
01:36:17,250 --> 01:36:20,250
Just a 20% discount from the shoe store.

1147
01:36:24,625 --> 01:36:26,291
I have enough shoes at home.

1148
01:36:36,125 --> 01:36:38,750
I wish I'd known
what "enough" meant back then.

1149
01:36:42,500 --> 01:36:44,750
My brother would be alive now.

1150
01:36:49,750 --> 01:36:53,291
I should be responsible
for making you happy.

1151
01:36:53,375 --> 01:36:54,500
It's my fault.

1152
01:36:55,875 --> 01:36:59,750
I should've known that you were sad
because your dad sold the house.

1153
01:37:00,375 --> 01:37:03,583
He never learns. He's too stubborn.

1154
01:37:04,291 --> 01:37:06,375
Nothing's ever good enough for him.

1155
01:37:08,875 --> 01:37:10,166
Well, maybe…

1156
01:37:13,375 --> 01:37:16,000
he feels good enough with himself,

1157
01:37:16,083 --> 01:37:19,416
but he doesn't feel good enough
to be your dad.

1158
01:38:04,041 --> 01:38:07,791
LAND OWNERSHIP CERTIFICATE

1159
01:38:54,166 --> 01:38:56,666
CONGRATULATIONS TO OUR NEW MEMBERS

1160
01:38:57,458 --> 01:38:59,166
I want you to know something.

1161
01:38:59,250 --> 01:39:02,583
When you were putting me in a trance,
I felt happy.

1162
01:39:04,166 --> 01:39:06,125
So you have to believe in yourself.

1163
01:39:07,125 --> 01:39:08,625
You're a good spirit channeler.

1164
01:39:11,166 --> 01:39:12,166
Good luck.

1165
01:39:16,375 --> 01:39:19,375
Wow, new flute!

1166
01:39:20,250 --> 01:39:21,541
New flute.

1167
01:39:24,791 --> 01:39:26,791
It's from my dad.

1168
01:39:27,916 --> 01:39:29,333
He made it with a water pipe.

1169
01:39:29,416 --> 01:39:31,333
The day has finally come.

1170
01:39:31,416 --> 01:39:35,625
Welcome to Latas Village's
grand trance party!

1171
01:39:37,708 --> 01:39:40,416
All the profits from today

1172
01:39:40,500 --> 01:39:43,416
will be used to buy the spring
from Mr. Dawuri.

1173
01:39:44,375 --> 01:39:47,541
After conducting a selection process
in eight schools in Latas,

1174
01:39:47,625 --> 01:39:50,541
I'd like to introduce you
to the new spirit channeler.

1175
01:39:50,625 --> 01:39:54,083
He'll be leading today's party.
With you, Ananto Prasetya!

1176
01:39:55,333 --> 01:39:56,791
Let's go, Ananto!

1177
01:39:56,875 --> 01:40:02,000
And his two assistants,
Pawit Arifin and Bayu Laksana!

1178
01:40:05,500 --> 01:40:07,625
The tiger's out for lunch!

1179
01:40:07,708 --> 01:40:10,916
Don't hold back, land a punch!

1180
01:40:52,250 --> 01:40:54,583
What are those security guards doing here?

1181
01:41:10,500 --> 01:41:13,625
Who's that guy? Do you know him?

1182
01:41:34,541 --> 01:41:35,625
Help!

1183
01:41:35,708 --> 01:41:37,583
- A host attacked a man!
- Lies!

1184
01:41:38,208 --> 01:41:40,291
- We have it on video.
- He's not in a trance!

1185
01:41:40,375 --> 01:41:42,083
<i>A host attacked a villager!</i>

1186
01:41:42,166 --> 01:41:44,833
Don't touch the hosts!

1187
01:41:44,916 --> 01:41:46,916
Hosts, do not attack!

1188
01:41:47,000 --> 01:41:50,250
<i>One of the hosts attacked a villager.</i>

1189
01:41:50,333 --> 01:41:52,958
<i>There's video evidence.</i>
<i>They are causing a disturbance!</i>

1190
01:41:54,875 --> 01:41:59,416
<i>All villagers, please evacuate the area.</i>

1191
01:41:59,500 --> 01:42:02,291
<i>One of the hosts attacked a villager!</i>

1192
01:42:02,375 --> 01:42:04,000
Go! Go! Go!

1193
01:42:05,000 --> 01:42:09,125
<i>All villagers, please evacuate the area.</i>

1194
01:42:10,125 --> 01:42:13,916
<i>One of the hosts attacked a villager!</i>

1195
01:42:14,000 --> 01:42:19,250
<i>This parties have caused disturbances</i>
<i>over and over again!</i>

1196
01:42:19,791 --> 01:42:24,416
<i>- Please evacuate the area!</i>
- How dare you? This is all a lie!

1197
01:42:24,500 --> 01:42:29,750
<i>All villagers, please evacuate the area.</i>

1198
01:42:30,375 --> 01:42:34,416
<i>One of the hosts attacked a villager!</i>

1199
01:42:34,500 --> 01:42:39,166
<i>This parties have caused disturbances</i>
<i>over and over again!</i>

1200
01:42:40,125 --> 01:42:43,375
<i>Please evacuate the area!</i>

1201
01:42:44,375 --> 01:42:48,916
<i>All villagers, please evacuate the area.</i>

1202
01:42:52,250 --> 01:42:54,041
Guru Asri, sing the turtle mantra!

1203
01:42:54,125 --> 01:42:56,916
Pawit and Ananto, get all the hosts!

1204
01:42:58,916 --> 01:43:01,416
Turtle self-protection forevermore!

1205
01:43:01,500 --> 01:43:04,750
Protected at the core!

1206
01:43:29,000 --> 01:43:30,541
Guru Asri, the massage realm!

1207
01:43:38,625 --> 01:43:41,416
Bayu, get everyone in!

1208
01:43:52,541 --> 01:43:56,458
The rattan stick, Bayu!
Protect their backs!

1209
01:44:09,500 --> 01:44:12,791
<i>Laksmi, forgive me for walking out on you.</i>

1210
01:44:12,875 --> 01:44:16,166
<i>Ananto, I'm sorry</i>
<i>for treating you as a rival.</i>

1211
01:44:16,250 --> 01:44:18,666
<i>Pawit, thank you</i>
<i>for always being there for me.</i>

1212
01:44:19,708 --> 01:44:22,291
<i>Ma'am, thank you for always guiding me.</i>

1213
01:44:23,166 --> 01:44:26,666
<i>People of Latas,</i>
<i>forgive me for being selfish.</i>

1214
01:44:33,125 --> 01:44:36,041
<i>Human statue from my past,</i>

1215
01:44:37,000 --> 01:44:40,166
<i>thank you for going through all that.</i>

1216
01:44:41,750 --> 01:44:43,666
<i>Thank you for pushing forward.</i>

1217
01:44:44,500 --> 01:44:47,000
The turtle's shell withstands the stick!

1218
01:45:52,375 --> 01:45:55,041
Ananto, the ant spirit!
Pawit, form the host circle!

1219
01:45:55,125 --> 01:45:56,666
Are you sure?

1220
01:45:56,750 --> 01:45:58,583
Ants scurrying all around!

1221
01:45:58,666 --> 01:46:01,375
Get tangled in your hair
and move all round!

1222
01:46:33,250 --> 01:46:36,958
Bayu! The fire ant spirit
will see the security guards as prey!

1223
01:46:39,125 --> 01:46:40,416
You want to attack them?

1224
01:46:42,458 --> 01:46:44,375
No, nobody will hurt anyone!

1225
01:46:47,250 --> 01:46:49,666
<i>You could use the leech spirit.</i>

1226
01:46:49,750 --> 01:46:53,791
<i>Destroy all those security guards,</i>
<i>suck them dry.</i>

1227
01:46:53,875 --> 01:46:55,625
<i>They deserve it.</i>

1228
01:46:56,375 --> 01:46:58,416
<i>No, no, no.</i>

1229
01:46:58,500 --> 01:47:01,041
<i>Not like that.</i>

1230
01:47:02,041 --> 01:47:04,416
<i>Bayu, he might not be a bad person.</i>

1231
01:47:04,916 --> 01:47:07,125
<i>Maybe he's just following orders.</i>

1232
01:47:08,875 --> 01:47:13,916
<i>He might not harbor hatred in his heart.</i>
<i>Maybe he has a family to feed.</i>

1233
01:47:15,375 --> 01:47:20,416
<i>He might not be a murderer.</i>
<i>Maybe he has a sick father at home.</i>

1234
01:47:21,416 --> 01:47:22,791
<i>They just need to be hugged.</i>

1235
01:47:33,166 --> 01:47:35,750
<i>This guy might not be a bad man after all.</i>

1236
01:47:36,375 --> 01:47:38,291
<i>Maybe he just needs to prove something.</i>

1237
01:47:39,125 --> 01:47:41,791
<i>Maybe he's been hurt.</i>
<i>Taken for granted, like me.</i>

1238
01:47:41,875 --> 01:47:44,041
<i>Maybe he feels he's not good enough.</i>

1239
01:47:47,875 --> 01:47:50,625
<i>Dad has always been alone.</i>

1240
01:47:51,375 --> 01:47:55,125
<i>He was jailed and beaten up</i>
<i>because he stole a phone.</i>

1241
01:47:56,250 --> 01:47:59,666
<i>After we both starved,</i>
<i>his wife walked out on him.</i>

1242
01:47:59,750 --> 01:48:01,500
<i>He kept getting scammed.</i>

1243
01:48:02,125 --> 01:48:03,791
<i>His plant business failed.</i>

1244
01:48:03,875 --> 01:48:05,333
<i>His gemstone business failed.</i>

1245
01:48:05,416 --> 01:48:07,333
<i>His betta fish business failed.</i>

1246
01:48:07,416 --> 01:48:09,708
<i>Dad did all of that for me.</i>

1247
01:48:09,791 --> 01:48:14,416
<i>Maybe he felt good about himself,</i>
<i>but he hasn't felt good enough as my dad.</i>

1248
01:48:14,500 --> 01:48:16,041
<i>I'm sorry, Dad.</i>

1249
01:48:16,125 --> 01:48:19,000
<i>Thank you. You're not alone.</i>

1250
01:48:35,250 --> 01:48:36,791
I can't hold it anymore!

1251
01:48:38,333 --> 01:48:41,916
Monkey spirit!
Remember your training for the monkey hug!

1252
01:48:48,416 --> 01:48:53,500
- A monkey eats a banana under a rug!
- Come on, get them in a group hug!

1253
01:49:18,958 --> 01:49:23,958
<i>We're already waiting by the gate.</i>
<i>Please wait.</i>

1254
01:49:24,041 --> 01:49:29,416
<i>Ten people are heading up.</i>
<i>They'll be there in five minutes.</i>

1255
01:49:29,500 --> 01:49:30,916
<i>Copy that.</i>

1256
01:49:31,000 --> 01:49:33,708
I'd like to use this opportunity
to make it clear

1257
01:49:33,791 --> 01:49:37,791
that the Wanaria group had nothing to do

1258
01:49:37,875 --> 01:49:41,958
with the incident that occurred
during yesterday's trance party.

1259
01:49:42,041 --> 01:49:47,291
We never gave such orders
and we condemn the perpetrators.

1260
01:49:47,375 --> 01:49:51,458
We believe some individuals from our old
security company were involved

1261
01:49:51,541 --> 01:49:54,666
in personal disputes with the villagers.

1262
01:49:54,750 --> 01:49:58,166
We at the Wanaria Group
have terminated our contract

1263
01:49:58,250 --> 01:50:00,541
with the security agency involved.

1264
01:50:00,625 --> 01:50:04,041
We have also recruited
a new security agency.

1265
01:50:04,125 --> 01:50:09,416
We want to preserve the culture
of trance parties in Latas Village.

1266
01:50:10,041 --> 01:50:15,375
Why? So that local tourists
and foreign tourists can come here.

1267
01:50:16,375 --> 01:50:21,791
We're also considering promoting it
as an international attraction.

1268
01:50:21,875 --> 01:50:23,500
Liar! Liar!

1269
01:50:23,583 --> 01:50:27,125
- Wanaria was behind it all along!
- We want the truth!

1270
01:50:51,875 --> 01:50:53,375
We are grateful.

1271
01:50:54,375 --> 01:50:57,791
The spring didn't fall
into Wanaria's hands.

1272
01:50:57,875 --> 01:51:03,458
But we have to realize
that our fight is far from over.

1273
01:51:04,625 --> 01:51:05,916
Wanaria is still here!

1274
01:51:06,000 --> 01:51:11,958
And what we are doing here
is a form of resistance against them.

1275
01:52:26,875 --> 01:52:29,583
Bayu, do you want some tea,
coffee, or orange juice?

1276
01:52:29,666 --> 01:52:31,291
Water's fine.

1277
01:52:36,250 --> 01:52:38,625
So Ananto was chosen
as the spirit channeler?

1278
01:52:38,708 --> 01:52:43,583
Yes. But it's okay. In the end,
they didn't do anything to his rice field.

1279
01:52:43,666 --> 01:52:46,833
It's all right. You'll get another chance.

1280
01:52:47,958 --> 01:52:48,916
Yes.

1281
01:52:49,875 --> 01:52:50,750
How's the house?

1282
01:52:50,833 --> 01:52:54,958
Good. They left our side yard intact.

1283
01:52:55,541 --> 01:53:00,041
Due to the incident, some restaurateurs
looking to invest changed their minds.

1284
01:53:00,125 --> 01:53:02,291
They just left.

1285
01:53:02,375 --> 01:53:03,541
All right.

1286
01:53:04,250 --> 01:53:06,166
These are Mrs. Nana's children.

1287
01:53:06,250 --> 01:53:07,375
Hello.

1288
01:53:07,458 --> 01:53:09,416
- Hello.
- Hey.

1289
01:53:09,500 --> 01:53:11,875
- Uncle, we'll go play soccer.
- Okay, be careful.

1290
01:53:11,958 --> 01:53:13,000
Okay.

1291
01:53:13,625 --> 01:53:16,291
They're calling you uncle now?

1292
01:53:17,250 --> 01:53:19,375
They're not used to calling me dad yet.

1293
01:53:22,625 --> 01:53:25,166
So what spirit do you have now?

1294
01:53:26,000 --> 01:53:27,916
- The lizard.
- Wow.

1295
01:53:28,000 --> 01:53:29,333
Just got it yesterday.

1296
01:53:29,416 --> 01:53:33,416
The lizard is cool. Upper rank.

1297
01:53:33,500 --> 01:53:34,875
Do you want to try it?

1298
01:53:38,000 --> 01:53:39,000
What do you mean?

1299
01:53:39,583 --> 01:53:41,000
The lizard spirit.

1300
01:53:41,916 --> 01:53:46,833
The last time you were a host
was 20, 30 years ago?

1301
01:53:47,500 --> 01:53:48,416
It's been 35 years.

1302
01:53:48,500 --> 01:53:50,500
That's like forever.

1303
01:53:52,125 --> 01:53:55,791
Want to try it? I got my flute with me.

1304
01:53:59,041 --> 01:54:01,375
I'm still here for the weekend.

1305
01:54:02,000 --> 01:54:03,916
I'll go back to Latas on Monday.

1306
01:54:14,625 --> 01:54:17,250
"SKR" DRINKING WATER
HIGH-QUALITY REFILLS

1307
01:54:31,375 --> 01:54:32,791
I'll skip the soup.

1308
01:54:33,875 --> 01:54:36,250
Better to do this on an empty stomach.

1309
01:54:37,875 --> 01:54:38,875
Shall we?



